<p data-start="4334" data-end="4381">In RSVP simulations, TP-like modules integrate:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>500</mn><mtext>&nbsp;ms</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t \in [0, 500\text{ ms}]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6542em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">500</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">&nbsp;ms</span></span><span class="mclose">]</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4415" data-end="4460">before updating the global semantic manifold.</p>
<p data-start="4462" data-end="4521">The empirical data match those timescales <em data-start="4504" data-end="4520">almost exactly</em>.</p>
<hr data-start="4523" data-end="4526">
<h1 data-start="4528" data-end="4614"><strong data-start="4530" data-end="4614">6. Layer–Time Alignment Interrupts Predictability → RSVP's Stability Under Error</strong></h1>
<p data-start="4616" data-end="4643">The study shows the effect:</p>
<ul data-start="4645" data-end="4727">
<li data-start="4645" data-end="4693">
<p data-start="4647" data-end="4693">Holds even for <em data-start="4662" data-end="4685">incorrectly predicted</em> words</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4694" data-end="4727">
<p data-start="4696" data-end="4727">Weakens but does not collapse</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4729" data-end="4764">In RSVP, semantic fields evolve as:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Prediction&nbsp;error&nbsp;modulates&nbsp;S,&nbsp;but&nbsp;does&nbsp;not&nbsp;reset&nbsp;Φ–v&nbsp;structure</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Prediction error modulates S, but does not reset Φ–v structure}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Prediction&nbsp;error&nbsp;modulates&nbsp;S,&nbsp;but&nbsp;does&nbsp;not&nbsp;reset&nbsp;Φ–v&nbsp;structure</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4843" data-end="4925">Prediction error adjusts entropy (S-field), but the recursive flow still proceeds.</p>
<p data-start="4927" data-end="4958">This is another direct mapping.</p>
<hr data-start="4960" data-end="4963">
<h1 data-start="4965" data-end="5026"><strong data-start="4967" data-end="5026">7. The Authors Suggest Recurrence → RSVP Already Has It</strong></h1>
<p data-start="5028" data-end="5050">The paper argues that:</p>
<ul data-start="5052" data-end="5176">
<li data-start="5052" data-end="5106">
<p data-start="5054" data-end="5106">Pure feed-forward Transformers may be insufficient</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5107" data-end="5176">
<p data-start="5109" data-end="5176">Recurrent or hybrid architectures may better match brain dynamics</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5178" data-end="5223">RSVP is already a <strong data-start="5196" data-end="5222">recurrent field theory</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="5225" data-end="5389">
<li data-start="5225" data-end="5270">
<p data-start="5227" data-end="5270">Φ, v, S are updated iteratively across time</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5271" data-end="5311">
<p data-start="5273" data-end="5311">Recurrence is intrinsic, not bolted on</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5312" data-end="5389">
