ull min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="377003bf-b4be-4fdd-8ac1-3c310c5cbf89" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="331">Below is a <strong data-start="11" data-end="54">complete, publication-ready draft paper</strong> titled<br data-start="61" data-end="64">
<strong data-start="64" data-end="150"><em data-start="66" data-end="148">Temporal Hierarchies in Cortical Language Processing as Recursive Field Dynamics</em></strong>,<br data-start="151" data-end="154">
integrating the empirical findings of Goldstein et al. (Nature Communications, 2025) with the theoretical architecture of the Relativistic Scalar-Vector Plenum (RSVP) framework.</p>
<p data-start="333" data-end="591">It is written in clean academic prose, structured like a neuroscience + theoretical modeling article, with explicit claims, equations, and predictions. No diagrams. You can later request a full LaTeX version, references.bib file, or journal-style formatting.</p>
<hr data-start="593" data-end="596">
<h1 data-start="598" data-end="686"><strong data-start="600" data-end="684">Temporal Hierarchies in Cortical Language Processing as Recursive Field Dynamics</strong></h1>
<p data-start="687" data-end="777"><strong data-start="687" data-end="777">A Theoretical Interpretation of Layer–Time Isomorphism in Human Language Comprehension</strong></p>
<p data-start="779" data-end="812"><strong data-start="779" data-end="805">Nate Guimond (Flyxion)</strong><br data-start="805" data-end="808">
2025</p>
<hr data-start="814" data-end="817">
<h2 data-start="819" data-end="834"><strong data-start="822" data-end="834">Abstract</strong></h2>
<p data-start="836" data-end="2278">Recent intracranial electrocorticography (ECoG) findings demonstrate a robust, monotonic correspondence between the depth of layers in large language models (LLMs) and the temporal progression of neural responses in high-order human language areas. Deeper LLM layers systematically align with later neural latencies in inferior frontal gyrus (IFG) and temporal pole (TP), while early auditory cortex shows no such mapping. This paper develops a formal theoretical interpretation of these findings using the Relativistic Scalar-Vector Plenum (RSVP) framework—a field-theoretic model of semantic and cognitive computation. RSVP predicts that language comprehension unfolds through recursive updates of three interacting fields: the semantic potential <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span>, the vectorial agency field <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span>, and the entropy field <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span>. These fields evolve through nonlinear transformations over time, forming widening temporal receptive windows that integrate information across phonetic, syntactic, and semantic scales. The empirical layer–time isomorphism observed in human cortex matches RSVP’s temporal-dilational geometry, validates its rejection of symbolic decomposition, and provides a direct neural signature of recursive field evolution. We formalize this mapping, derive testable predictions, and propose a unified neurocomputational interpretation of language processing as a lamphrodynamic relaxation process in the semantic manifold.</p>
<hr data-start="2280" data-end="2283">
<h1 data-start="2285" data-end="2306"><strong data-start="2287" data-end="2306">1. Introduction</strong></h1>
<p data-start="2308" data-end="2736">Understanding how the brain constructs meaning from continuous speech requires a model that links <strong data-start="2406" data-end="2434">temporal neural dynamics</strong>, <strong data-start="2436" data-end="2472">representational transformations</strong>, and <strong data-start="2478" data-end="2529">structured integration across linguistic levels</strong>. Traditional symbolic theories have posited discrete operations—phoneme extraction, morphosyntactic parsing, semantic combination—yet empirical evidence increasingly contradicts such stepwise architectures.</p>
<p data-start="2738" data-end="3063">A recent ECoG study (Goldstein et al., 2025) reveals a striking relationship between the brain's temporal unfolding of language and the structural hierarchy of modern large language models (LLMs). Deeper LLM layers correlate with progressively later neural responses in IFG and TP, forming a nearly linear layer–time mapping.</p>
<p data-start="3065" data-end="3327">This result is theoretically significant. It suggests that the brain does not process linguistic units discretely; instead, it evolves internal representations through <strong data-start="3233" data-end="3272">iterative nonlinear transformations</strong>, analogous to the stacked computational steps in LLMs.</p>
<p data-start="3329" data-end="3510">Here we argue that this phenomenon is precisely what the RSVP framework predicts. RSVP models cognition as the evolution of a semantic plenum consisting of three interacting fields:</p>
<ul data-start="3512" data-end="3661">
<li data-start="3512" data-end="3544">
<p data-start="3514" data-end="3544"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span>: semantic potential</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3545" data-end="3599">
<p data-start="3547" data-end="3599"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span>: vector field of directed inference</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3600" data-end="3661">
<p data-start="3602" data-end="3661"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span>: entropy field regulating uncertainty and integration</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3663" data-end="3946">Language comprehension, in RSVP, is the recursive transformation of these fields over time. We show that the empirical findings map directly onto the temporal geometry of RSVP’s lamphrodynamic equations and derive new predictions that extend beyond current LLMs and cognitive models.</p>
<hr data-start="3948" data-end="3951">
<h1 data-start="3953" data-end="3972"><strong data-start="3955" data-end="3972">2. Background</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start="3974" data-end="4035"><strong data-start="3977" data-end="4035">2.1 Temporal structure of cortical language processing</strong></h2>
<p data-start="4037" data-end="4119">Cortical language pathways exhibit a known gradient of temporal receptive windows:</p>
<ul data-start="4121" data-end="4236">
<li data-start="4121" data-end="4140">
<p data-start="4123" data-end="4140">mSTG: ~10–50 ms</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4141" data-end="4162">
<p data-start="4143" data-end="4162">aSTG: ~100–200 ms</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4163" data-end="4184">
<p data-start="4165" data-end="4184">IFG: ~200–400+ ms</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4185" data-end="4236">
<p data-start="4187" data-end="4236">TP: ~300–500+ ms, long-range semantic integration</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4238" data-end="4321">Goldstein et al. show that these windows align systematically with LLM layer depth:</p>
<ul data-start="4323" data-end="4440">
<li data-start="4323" data-end="4380">
<p data-start="4325" data-end="4380">early layers → early windows → early auditory regions</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4381" data-end="4440">
<p data-start="4383" data-end="4440">deep layers → late windows → semantic hubs such as IFG/TP</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4442" data-end="4555">This layer–time gradient suggests a continuous representational refinement rather than discrete symbolic parsing.</p>
<h2 data-start="4557" data-end="4586"><strong data-start="4560" data-end="4586">2.2 The RSVP framework</strong></h2>
<p data-start="4588" data-end="4720">RSVP treats cognition as a dynamical system on a <strong data-start="4637" data-end="4658">semantic manifold</strong> governed by fields <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span>. These evolve via:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Phi_t, \mathbf{v}_t, S_t) \rightarrow (\Phi_{t+\delta}, \mathbf{v}_{t+\delta}, S_{t+\delta})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.016em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.016em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4824" data-end="4852">through nonlinear couplings:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mtable rowspacing="0.25em" columnalign="right left" columnspacing="0em"><mtr><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel="0" displaystyle="true"><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel="0" displaystyle="true"><mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub></mrow></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel="0" displaystyle="true"><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel="0" displaystyle="true"><mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel="0" displaystyle="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel="0" displaystyle="true"><mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{aligned}
