59em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style="top: -1.5798em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span><span class="mord">∥∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ϵ</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">ζS</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">η</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 2.0802em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="5166" data-end="5374">These are not literal cortical PDEs but <strong data-start="5206" data-end="5233">computational analogues</strong> of recursive representational dynamics. Language comprehension corresponds to recursive relaxation toward a coherent semantic configuration.</p>
<hr data-start="5376" data-end="5379">
<h1 data-start="5381" data-end="5440"><strong data-start="5383" data-end="5440">3. Layer–Time Isomorphism as Recursive Field Dynamics</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start="5442" data-end="5489"><strong data-start="5445" data-end="5489">3.1 Empirical finding: monotonic mapping</strong></h2>
<p data-start="5491" data-end="5515">Goldstein et al. report:</p>
<ul data-start="5517" data-end="5716">
<li data-start="5517" data-end="5624">
<p data-start="5519" data-end="5583">In IFG: correlation between LLM layer index and neural latency</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.85</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r = 0.85, \quad p &lt; 10^{-13}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8389em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">0.85</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&lt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8641em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">0</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">−</span><span class="mord mtight">13</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
</li>
<li data-start="5625" data-end="5681">
<p data-start="5627" data-end="5681">Temporal pole shows the largest mapping span (~500 ms)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5682" data-end="5716">
<p data-start="5684" data-end="5716">Auditory cortex shows no mapping</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5718" data-end="5808">This pattern suggests a layered temporal recursion akin to stacked neural transformations.</p>
<h2 data-start="5810" data-end="5868"><strong data-start="5813" data-end="5868">3.2 RSVP interpretation: each "layer" is a timestep</strong></h2>
<p data-start="5870" data-end="5979">In RSVP, each recursive update corresponds to a local relaxation step of the semantic fields. The mapping is:</p>
<ul data-start="5981" data-end="6145">
<li data-start="5981" data-end="6032">
<p data-start="5983" data-end="6032">LLM layer depth <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span></span></span></span> ≈ RSVP recursion step <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="6033" data-end="6145">
<p data-start="6035" data-end="6145">Neural latency <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>peak</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{peak}}(L)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0361em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">peak</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> ≈ time required for fields to relax into a deeper semantic configuration</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6147" data-end="6181">A simple phenomenological mapping:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>peak</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{peak}}(L) = t_0 + \lambda \ln(1 + L/L_0)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0361em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">peak</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7651em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">ln</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="mord">/</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6240" data-end="6327">captures the diminishing marginal integration characteristic of lamphrodynamic updates.</p>
<h2 data-start="6329" data-end="6383"><strong data-start="6332" data-end="6383">3.3 Why the hierarchy is temporal, not symbolic</strong></h2>
<p data-start="6385" data-end="6420">Symbolic linguistic models predict:</p>
<ul data-start="6422" data-end="6521">
<li data-start="6422" data-end="6456">
<p data-start="6424" data-end="6456">operations ordered by category</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6457" data-end="6521">
<p data-start="6459" data-end="6521">discrete transitions (phoneme → morpheme → syntax → semantics)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6523" data-end="6598">But the empirical data show no such categorical boundaries. The mapping is:</p>
<ul data-start="6600" data-end="6639">
<li data-start="6600" data-end="6610">
<p data-start="6602" data-end="6610">smooth</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6611" data-end="6625">
<p data-start="6613" data-end="6625">continuous</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6626" data-end="6639">
<p data-start="6628" data-end="6639">monotonic</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6641" data-end="6774">in both the brain and LLMs. RSVP predicts this because semantic fields evolve continuously, not by symbolic firing of discrete rules.</p>
<hr data-start="6776" data-end="6779">
<h1 data-start="6781" data-end="6843"><strong data-start="6783" data-end="6843">4. Temporal Receptive Windows as Dilated Semantic Fields</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start="6845" data-end="6874"><strong data-start="6848" data-end="6874">4.1 The RSVP principle</strong></h2>
<p data-start="6876" data-end="6888">RSVP posits:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>integration</mtext></msub><mo>∝</mo><mtext>semantic&nbsp;depth</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t_{\text{integration}} \propto \text{semantic depth}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3175em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">integration</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">semantic&nbsp;depth</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6957" data-end="7106">As the semantic potential <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span> deepens, the entropy field <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> requires longer temporal windows to settle into a coherent low-entropy attractor.</p>
<h2 data-start="7108" data-end="7134"><strong data-start="7111" data-end="7134">4.2 Empirical match</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="7136" data-end="7245">
<li data-start="7136" data-end="7174">
<p data-start="7138" data-end="7174">mSTG: rapid, shallow field updates</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7175" data-end="7197">
<p data-start="7177" data-end="7197">aSTG: intermediate</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7198" data-end="7245">
<p data-start="7200" data-end="7245">IFG, TP: deepest attractors → largest windows</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="7247" data-end="7390">The IFG/TP findings align exactly with RSVP’s “deep-field reservoirs” where semantic ambiguity is resolved only after multiple recursive steps.</p>
<hr data-start="7392" data-end="7395">
<h1 data-start="7397" data-end="7455"><strong data-start="7399" data-end="7455">5. Nonlinearity, Entropy, and Semantic Stabilization</strong></h1>
<p data-start="7457" data-end="7611">A central empirical finding is that <strong data-start="7493" data-end="7522">nonlinear transformations</strong> across layers are necessary. Linear interpolation fails to reproduce the neural mapping.</p>
<p data-start="7613" data-end="7642">RSVP explains this naturally:</p>
<ul data-start="7644" data-end="7811">
<li data-start="7644" data-end="7707">
<p data-start="7646" data-end="7707"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span> evolves under nonlinear coupling with <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="7708" data-end="7763">
<p data-start="7710" data-end="7763"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span> exhibits vorticity and curvature terms</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7764" data-end="7811">
<p data-start="7766" data-end="7811"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> modulates the gain and depth of updates</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="7813" data-end="7940">Semantic stabilization requires these nonlinearities; linear models cannot produce the observed hierarchical temporal dynamics.</p>
<hr data-start="7942" data-end="7945">
<h1 data-start="7947" data-end="8004"><strong data-start="7949" data-end="8004">6. Prediction Error and Stability of Field Dynamics</strong></h1>
<p data-start="8006" data-end="8028">Goldstein et al. show:</p>
<ul data-start="8030" data-end="8127">
<li data-start="8030" data-end="8098">
<p data-start="8032" data-end="8098">Layer–time mapping persists even for incorrectly predicted words</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8099" data-end="8127">
<p data-start="8101" data-end="8127">Only weakened in magnitude</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="8129" data-end="8167">RSVP predicts this robustness because:</p>
<ul data-start="8169" data-end="8312">
<li data-start="8169" data-end="8214">
<p data-start="8171" data-end="8214">Prediction error modifies <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> (entropy)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8215" data-end="8263">
<p data-start="8217" data-end="8263">It does not reset <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span> or <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="8264" data-end="8312">
<p data-start="8266" data-end="8312">Semantic fields retain momentum and continuity</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="8314" data-end="8361">This contrasts with brittle symbolic pipelines.</p>
<hr data-start="8363" data-end="8366">
<h1 data-start="8368" data-end="8421"><strong data-start="8370" data-end="8421">7. Implications for Neurocomputational Modeling</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start="8423" data-end="8472"><strong data-start="8426" data-end="8472">7.1 LLMs as partial field-theoretic models</strong></h2>
<p data-start="8474" data-end="8588">LLMs approximate iterative refinement via stacked feed-forward layers. RSVP interprets these as discrete steps of:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">R</mi><mo>:</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>↦</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">′</mo></msup><mo separator="true">,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">′</mo></msup><mo separator="true">,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}: (\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S) \mapsto (\Phi', \mathbf{v}', S')</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">R</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">↦</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0519em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8019em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8019em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8019em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="8665" data-end="8837">Their alignment with cortical dynamics suggests that deep learning—and particularly large-scale Transformers—learn structures that match biological recursive field updates.</p>
<h2 data-start="8839" data-end="8884"><strong data-start="8842" data-end="8884">7.2 Recurrence as a missing ingredient</strong></h2>
<p data-start="8886" data-end="8986">Transformers lack explicit temporal recurrence. RSVP argues that true cortical computation requires:</p>
<ul data-start="8988" data-end="9077">
<li data-start="8988" data-end="9014">
<p data-start="8990" data-end="9014">field-based recurrence</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9015" data-end="9043">
<p data-start="9017" data-end="9043">lamphrodynamic smoothing</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9044" data-end="9077">
<p data-start="9046" data-end="9077">entropy-weighted update inertia</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="9079" data-end="9174">A hybrid architecture could combine the strengths of LLMs with RSVP’s dynamic field principles.</p>
<hr data-start="9176" data-end="9179">
<h1 data-start="9181" data-end="9228"><strong data-start="9183" data-end="9228">8. Predictions and Experimental Proposals</strong></h1>
<h3 data-start="9230" data-end="9292"><strong data-start="9234" data-end="9292">Prediction 1: Vorticity signatures in ambiguous syntax</strong></h3>
<p data-start="9293" data-end="9447">During syntactic ambiguity, RSVP predicts transient increases in the rotational component of <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span>. MEG/eyetracking correlations could test this.</p>
<h3 data-start="9449" data-end="9512"><strong data-start="9453" data-end="9512">Prediction 2: Entropy peaks precede semantic resolution</strong></h3>
<p data-start="9513" data-end="9596">RSVP predicts a rise in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> ~100–200 ms before resolution of ambiguity in TP/IFG.</p>
<h3 data-start="9598" data-end="9662"><strong data-start="9602" data-end="9662">Prediction 3: Recursive attractors for narrative closure</strong></h3>
<p data-start="9663" data-end="9783">Ending a narrative should collapse <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span> and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> into low-entropy attractors measurable as synchronized late peaks.</p>
<h3 data-start="9785" data-end="9835"><strong data-start="9789" data-end="9835">Prediction 4: Scaling with discourse depth</strong></h3>
<p data-start="9836" data-end="9943">Longer narrative dependencies should shift the layer–time curve upward proportionally to semantic distance.</p>
<hr data-start="9945" data-end="9948">
<h1 data-start="9950" data-end="9969"><strong data-start="9952" data-end="9969">9. Conclusion</strong></h1>
<p data-start="9971" data-end="10477">The empirical layer–time hierarchy uncovered in high-order language cortex provides a direct neural signature of recursive semantic processing. The Relativistic Scalar-Vector Plenum framework interprets this as evidence that the brain constructs meaning through iterative field evolution, not symbolic rule application. The alignment between cortical temporal dynamics and LLM architectural depth supports a unified view of language as a lamphrodynamic relaxation process in a structured semantic manifold.</p>
<p data-start="10479" data-end="10728">RSVP thus offers both an explanatory bridge and a generative blueprint for next-generation neuro-AI systems—models that process language through continuous, recurrent, energy-constrained field dynamics analogous to those observed in the human brain.</p>
<hr data-start="10730" data-end="10733">
