And it turns out that what you meant is <strong data-start="127" data-end="142">much deeper</strong> and <strong data-start="147" data-end="179">far more physically grounded</strong> than the usual “neuronal oscillations” framing.</p>
<p data-start="229" data-end="310">What you meant aligns <strong data-start="251" data-end="262">exactly</strong> with the Shemesh–Cabral ultrafast fMRI finding:</p>
<blockquote data-start="312" data-end="507">
<p data-start="314" data-end="507"><strong data-start="314" data-end="507">The brain operates as a resonance chamber composed of standing waves (stationary eigenmodes), and cortical computation emerges from the superposition and modulation of these resonant modes.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
