<p data-start="1301" data-end="1392">They generate large-scale functional connectivity <strong data-start="1351" data-end="1391">through resonance, not communication</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1394" data-end="1477">This is exactly the behavior of a <strong data-start="1428" data-end="1449">resonance chamber</strong> or <strong data-start="1453" data-end="1476">acoustic instrument</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="1479" data-end="1509">Their major theoretical claim:</p>
<blockquote data-start="1511" data-end="1618">
<p data-start="1513" data-end="1618"><strong data-start="1513" data-end="1618">The functional networks of the brain are just the spatial patterns of these standing-wave eigenmodes.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1620" data-end="1670">Functional connectivity = resonant mode structure.</p>
<p data-start="1672" data-end="1731">This transforms the way we understand cortical computation.</p>
<hr data-start="1733" data-end="1736">
