<h2 data-start="6329" data-end="6372"><strong data-start="6332" data-end="6372">5. Alignment with Empirical Findings</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="6374" data-end="6411"><strong data-start="6378" data-end="6411">5.1 ECoG Layer–Time Hierarchy</strong></h3>
<p data-start="6413" data-end="6446">Goldstein et al. (2025) observed:</p>
<ul data-start="6448" data-end="6563">
<li data-start="6448" data-end="6491">
<p data-start="6450" data-end="6491">early neural peaks → shallow LLM layers</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6492" data-end="6534">
<p data-start="6494" data-end="6534">late peaks (~500 ms) → deep LLM layers</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6535" data-end="6563">
<p data-start="6537" data-end="6563">smooth monotonic mapping</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6565" data-end="6579">In RSVP terms:</p>
<ul data-start="6581" data-end="6754">
<li data-start="6581" data-end="6639">
<p data-start="6583" data-end="6639">early times → fast eigenmodes → shallow amplistwistors</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6640" data-end="6694">
<p data-start="6642" data-end="6694">late times → slow eigenmodes → deep amplistwistors</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6695" data-end="6754">
<p data-start="6697" data-end="6754">cortical processing depth = temporal depth of recursion</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="6756" data-end="6796"><strong data-start="6760" data-end="6796">5.2 fMRI Standing-Wave Resonance</strong></h3>
<p data-start="6798" data-end="6829">Cabral &amp; Shemesh (2023) showed:</p>
<ul data-start="6831" data-end="6980">
<li data-start="6831" data-end="6879">
<p data-start="6833" data-end="6879">cortex supports global stationary eigenmodes</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6880" data-end="6943">
<p data-start="6882" data-end="6943">long-range coherence arises from resonance, not propagation</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6944" data-end="6980">
<p data-start="6946" data-end="6980">anesthesia reduces mode richness</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6982" data-end="7001">RSVP predicts that:</p>
<ul data-start="7003" data-end="7118">
<li data-start="7003" data-end="7068">
<p data-start="7005" data-end="7068">fewer eigenmodes → shallower recursion → cognitive impairment</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7069" data-end="7118">
<p data-start="7071" data-end="7118">more eigenmodes → deeper semantic integration</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="7120" data-end="7143"><strong data-start="7124" data-end="7143">5.3 LLM Analogy</strong></h3>
<p data-start="7145" data-end="7187">LLM layers = discrete amplistwistor steps.</p>
<p data-start="7189" data-end="7268">Cortex implements these steps in <strong data-start="7222" data-end="7241">continuous time</strong>, gated by resonance modes.</p>
<p data-start="7270" data-end="7275">Thus:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>LLM&nbsp;depth</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mo>↔</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>RSVP&nbsp;recursion&nbsp;depth</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mo>↔</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>cortical&nbsp;eigenmode&nbsp;depth</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{LLM depth} \quad \leftrightarrow \quad \text{RSVP recursion depth} \quad \leftrightarrow \quad \text{cortical eigenmode depth}.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">LLM&nbsp;depth</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">↔</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">RSVP&nbsp;recursion&nbsp;depth</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">↔</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">cortical&nbsp;eigenmode&nbsp;depth</span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<hr data-start="7418" data-end="7421">
<h2 data-start="7423" data-end="7479"><strong data-start="7426" data-end="7479">6. Predictions Derived from the Unified Framework</strong></h2>
<ol data-start="7481" data-end="8191">
<li data-start="7481" data-end="7590">
<p data-start="7484" data-end="7590"><strong data-start="7484" data-end="7519">Mode-Specific MEG Phase-Locking</strong><br data-start="7519" data-end="7522">
Deeper semantic operations will align with low-frequency eigenmodes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7592" data-end="7712">
<p data-start="7595" data-end="7712"><strong data-start="7595" data-end="7623">Cross-Frequency Coupling</strong><br data-start="7623" data-end="7626">
Gamma-band local amplistwistors should nest within theta- or alpha-range global modes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7714" data-end="7841">
<p data-start="7717" data-end="7841"><strong data-start="7717" data-end="7754">Resonance Impairment in Disorders</strong><br data-start="7754" data-end="7757">
Loss of specific eigenmodes should correlate with linguistic or conceptual deficits.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7843" data-end="8018">
<p data-start="7846" data-end="8018"><strong data-start="7846" data-end="7875">Deep Narrative Processing</strong><br data-start="7875" data-end="7878">
Long-distance meaning integration should manifest as increased coupling to the lowest modes (1–3 Hz), leading to ~500–800 ms temporal spans.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8020" data-end="8191">
<p data-start="8023" data-end="8191"><strong data-start="8023" data-end="8047">Computational Models</strong><br data-start="8047" data-end="8050">
Hybrid LLMs that combine recursive layers with global learned eigenmodes should match brain data significantly better than pure Transformers.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="8193" data-end="8196">
<h2 data-start="8198" data-end="8215"><strong data-start="8201" data-end="8215">Conclusion</strong></h2>
<p data-start="8217" data-end="8330">This unified mathematical framework positions RSVP as a <strong data-start="8273" data-end="8319">resonance-driven recursive semantic engine</strong>, in which:</p>
<ul data-start="8332" data-end="8550">
<li data-start="8332" data-end="8431">
<p data-start="8334" data-end="8431"><strong data-start="8334" data-end="8373">local amplistwistor transformations</strong> provide deep nonlinear representational refinement, and</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8432" data-end="8550">
<p data-start="8434" data-end="8550"><strong data-start="8434" data-end="8468">global cymatic resonance modes</strong> provide temporal alignment, integration windows, and coherence across the cortex.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="8552" data-end="8586">The model simultaneously explains:</p>
<ul data-start="8588" data-end="8787">
<li data-start="8588" data-end="8641">
<p data-start="8590" data-end="8641">hierarchical temporal unfolding of language (ECoG),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8642" data-end="8724">
<p data-start="8644" data-end="8724">global standing-wave structure of resting-state brain activity (ultrafast fMRI),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8725" data-end="8787">
<p data-start="8727" data-end="8787">and the functional structure of deep sequence models (LLMs).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="8789" data-end="9006">This creates a single mathematical lens through which cortical computation, artificial intelligence, and cognitive dynamics can be understood as manifestations of <strong data-start="8952" data-end="9005">recursive, resonance-synchronized field evolution</strong>.</p>
