operations of scaling, rotation, and linear mixing of components. Under the
density assumption, arbitrary linear combinations of field values can be
generated. Projection then permits nonlinear shaping, creating a composition
scheme analogous to ridge-function networks. The Stone--Weierstrass theorem
extends to Banach-valued continuous functions, yielding density.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Universal Approximation Theorem}

We now state the main theorem of this section.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Universal Approximation]
