</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\left</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>
F(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span>)
-
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{A}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdots</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{A}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span>)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\right</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>
&lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\varepsilon</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}
By the density lemma, the algebra generated by amplistwistors is dense in
