</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">%=====================================================================</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Functional-Analytic Framework}

The analysis of the RSVP system requires a rigorous functional-analytic
foundation on the underlying Riemannian manifold </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}, g)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. Since
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dim</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})=2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, several embeddings and inequalities take particularly
favorable forms.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Sobolev Spaces}

For </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>s </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{N}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> p &lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, define the Sobolev space
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>W</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{s,p}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> in local coordinate patches and glue using partitions of
unity. Equivalently, define the Sobolev norm via covariant derivatives:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>u</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{W</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{s,p}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>p
=
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{k=0}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>s
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}} |</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>k u|</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>p </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> d</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{vol}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

We will primarily use </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>s = W</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{s,2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, denoting </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>0 = L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Sobolev Embedding Theorems on a 2-Manifold}

Since </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dim</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}=2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, we have:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Sobolev Embedding in Dimension Two]
Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>s &gt; 0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>p </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> 1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>sp &gt; 2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, then </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>W</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{s,p}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hookrightarrow</span></span><span> C</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>0(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>s = 1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>p=2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, then for all </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>q &lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
    H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hookrightarrow</span></span><span> L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}).
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> (Moser–Trudinger) For </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>u </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with 
    </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g u</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> 1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\exp</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span> u</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> d</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{vol}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g &lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{for all } </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span> &lt; 4</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

These embeddings will be used for controlling nonlinear terms involving
products and compositions of fields.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Gagliardo–Nirenberg Inequalities}

For </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>u </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>u</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>p}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span>
C </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>u</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{1-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g u</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> p &lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>,
