Under the assumption that </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is trace class on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>5</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the RSVP
system admits a unique stochastic mild solution
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>; C([0,T]; H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>5)).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Smoothing Properties of the Semigroup}

Because </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>c</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> dominates </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{L}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Parabolic Smoothing]
For </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t&gt;0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the semigroup satisfies:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span> e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{L}} u </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>k}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span>
C</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{k,t} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>u</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\forall</span></span><span> k </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{N}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

This is crucial for bootstrapping regularity in Section 6.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">%=====================================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% SECTION 6 — REGULARITY, ENERGY ESTIMATES, AND GLOBAL EXISTENCE</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">%=====================================================================</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Regularity, Energy Estimates, and Global Existence}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Higher Regularity}

Using parabolic bootstrapping:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}
If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>s</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, then for all </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t&gt;0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span>(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{s+2}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Energy Functional}

Define the energy
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
E(t)
=
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{1}{2}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2
+
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{1}{2}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vb</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2
+
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{1}{2}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Differentiating,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{dE}{dt}
=
c</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>
+
c</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>5</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vb</span></span><span>{v}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{curl}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vb</span></span><span>{v})</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>
-
c</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>9</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2
+
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span>, N(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>
+
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Using:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> u, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g u</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span> = -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> u</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
and skew-adjointness of curl:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vb</span></span><span>{v}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{curl}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vb</span></span><span>{v})</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span> = 0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
we obtain:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{dE}{dt}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span>
- c</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2
-
c</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>9</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{L</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2
+
C(1 + E(t)).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Gronwall Argument}

A standard Gronwall inequality yields:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Global Existence]
For initial data </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>5</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the RSVP system admits a
global solution
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> C([0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>); H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>5)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cap</span></span><span>
C((0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>); H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>k(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>5)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\forall</span></span><span> k </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{N}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

Thus no finite-time blow-up occurs under biologically realistic assumptions.

