</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>g </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{A}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span>)
=
D</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Big</span></span><span>[
(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Big</span></span><span>].
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Each term is Lipschitz on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> because </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>D</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
are uniformly bounded there. The estimate follows.
