    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> It is closed under conjugation by smooth diffeomorphisms.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

Thus </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{A}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ast</span></span><span>}=C</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Approximation in Sobolev Norm}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Universal Approximation in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>]
For any </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M};</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>d)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\varepsilon</span></span><span>&gt;0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, there
exists an amplistwistor cascade </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{A}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{(n)}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> such that
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span> - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{A}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{(n)}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Psi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1} &lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\varepsilon</span></span><span>.
