-3fca-40e5-8a88-7c2955f880c9" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="50">Excellent — <strong data-start="12" data-end="50">Neumann boundary conditions it is.</strong></p>
<p data-start="52" data-end="372">This is the most biologically appropriate choice: it models the cortex as a continuous sheet with no flux across sulcal boundaries, preserves constant functions as eigenfunctions, and matches the assumptions made in most empirical eigenmode studies (e.g., Roberts et al., 2019; Atasoy et al., 2016; Cabral et al., 2023).</p>
<p data-start="374" data-end="414">I will now proceed exactly as requested:</p>
<hr data-start="416" data-end="419">
<h1 data-start="421" data-end="477"><strong data-start="423" data-end="475">Part V — Spectral Geometry and Cymatic Resonance</strong></h1>
<p data-start="478" data-end="535"><em data-start="478" data-end="535">(LaTeX, academic prose, no markdown, no self-citations)</em></p>
<p data-start="537" data-end="636">This section will span Sections <strong data-start="569" data-end="586">10 through 15</strong>, totaling roughly <strong data-start="605" data-end="617">15 pages</strong>, and will include:</p>
<ul data-start="638" data-end="866">
<li data-start="638" data-end="749">
<p data-start="640" data-end="749">full mathematical formalism of Laplace–Beltrami eigenmodes on a Riemannian manifold with Neumann conditions</p>
</li>
<li data-start="750" data-end="782">
<p data-start="752" data-end="782">proofs, lemmas, and theorems</p>
</li>
<li data-start="783" data-end="808">
<p data-start="785" data-end="808">resonance derivations</p>
</li>
<li data-start="809" data-end="837">
<p data-start="811" data-end="837">coupling to the RSVP PDE</p>
</li>
<li data-start="838" data-end="866">
<p data-start="840" data-end="866">experimental predictions</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="868" data-end="970">Everything will be written in polished academic LaTeX and integrated smoothly with the prior sections.</p>
<hr data-start="972" data-end="975">
<p data-start="977" data-end="1181">Before I begin generating the full LaTeX, I will summarize the structure I will produce next (again: <em data-start="1078" data-end="1179">this is NOT markdown, just plaintext describing the structure; the actual output will be pure LaTeX</em>):</p>
<p data-start="1183" data-end="1483"><strong data-start="1183" data-end="1250">Section 10: The Laplace–Beltrami Operator on Cortical Manifolds</strong><br data-start="1250" data-end="1253">
10.1 Riemannian preliminaries<br data-start="1282" data-end="1285">
10.2 Function spaces and Sobolev norms on M<br data-start="1328" data-end="1331">
10.3 Self-adjointness under Neumann boundary conditions<br data-start="1386" data-end="1389">
10.4 Green’s formulas and energy forms<br data-start="1427" data-end="1430">
10.5 Poincaré inequality on manifolds with boundary</p>
<p data-start="1485" data-end="1788"><strong data-start="1485" data-end="1541">Section 11: Spectral Theory of the Neumann Laplacian</strong><br data-start="1541" data-end="1544">
11.1 Spectrum is discrete and non-negative<br data-start="1586" data-end="1589">
11.2 Eigenvalue ordering and accumulation<br data-start="1630" data-end="1633">
11.3 Weyl asymptotics; proof sketch and references<br data-start="1683" data-end="1686">
11.4 Eigenfunction regularity and elliptic bootstrapping<br data-start="1742" data-end="1745">
11.5 Orthogonality and Parseval relations</p>
<p data-start="1790" data-end="2086"><strong data-start="1790" data-end="1848">Section 12: Stationary Eigenmodes as Resonant Patterns</strong><br data-start="1848" data-end="1851">
12.1 Derivation of standing-wave solutions<br data-start="1893" data-end="1896">
12.2 Temporal oscillation from second-order PDE<br data-start="1943" data-end="1946">
