<p data-start="386" data-end="448">\section{The Laplace--Beltrami Operator on Cortical Manifolds}</p>
<p data-start="450" data-end="487">\subsection{Riemannian Preliminaries}</p>
<p data-start="489" data-end="1148">Let $(M,g)$ be a compact, connected, oriented $n$-dimensional Riemannian manifold with smooth boundary $\partial M$. The metric $g$ induces a natural inner product on tangent vectors, denoted $\langle \cdot,\cdot\rangle_g$, and a volume form $\mathrm{d}\mu_g$. All integration throughout this section will be taken with respect to $\mathrm{d}\mu_g$. We assume that $(M,g)$ satisfies standard geometric bounds: strictly positive injectivity radius, bounded sectional curvature, and finite volume. These conditions are satisfied by any cortical surface reconstructed from high-resolution MRI where the geometry is typically smoothed and numerically regularized.</p>
<p data-start="1150" data-end="1257">For a smooth function $u : M \to \mathbb{R}$, its gradient $\nabla u$ is the unique vector field satisfying</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>u</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}u(X)=\langle\nabla u,X\rangle_g</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathrm">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0361em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mopen">⟨</span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose"><span class="mclose">⟩</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">g</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1306" data-end="1397">for all smooth vector fields $X$ on $M$. The divergence of a vector field $X$ is defined by</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∂</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi></mrow></msqrt><mtext> </mtext><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{div}X = \frac1{\sqrt{|g|}} \partial_i\left(\sqrt{|g|}\,X^i\right),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mord mathrm" style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">div</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.4514em; vertical-align: -1.13em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3214em;"><span style="top: -2.175em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord sqrt"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.935em;"><span class="svg-align" style="top: -3.2em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.2em;"></span><span class="mord" style="padding-left: 1em;"><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="mar