<p data-start="411" data-end="461">\section{Spectral Theory of the Neumann Laplacian}</p>
<p data-start="463" data-end="512">\subsection{Discrete Spectrum and Non-Negativity}</p>
<p data-start="514" data-end="799">Let $-\Delta_N$ denote the Neumann Laplacian defined in the previous section. We recall that $-\Delta_N$ is a non-negative, self-adjoint operator with compact resolvent. By the spectral theorem for compact self-adjoint operators, the spectrum consists of a sequence of real eigenvalues</p>
