<p data-start="1111" data-end="1229">The eigenvalue $\lambda_0=0$ corresponds to the constant eigenfunctions. All higher eigenvalues are strictly positive.</p>
<p data-start="1231" data-end="1340">\begin{theorem}<br>
The set ${u_m}_{m=0}^\infty$ forms a complete orthonormal basis for $L^2(M)$.<br>
\end{theorem}</p>
<p data-start="1342" data-end="1562">\begin{proof}<br>
Compactness of the resolvent $(I-\Delta_N)^{-1}$ implies that $-\Delta_N$ has a complete set of $L^2$-orthonormal eigenfunctions. This is a classical consequence of the Hilbert--Schmidt theorem.<br>
\end{proof}</p>
<p data-start="1564" data-end="1616">\subsection{Minimax Characterization of Eigenvalues}</p>
<p data-start="1618" data-end="1705">The Courant--Fischer minimax principle gives a variational formula for the eigenvalues:</p>
