<p data-start="3221" data-end="3538">Higher-frequency eigenfunctions $u_m$ therefore contribute spatially finer oscillatory structure. This fact, combined with Weyl asymptotics, implies that the distribution of resonant spatial wavelengths is dense in the high-frequency limit, though physiological attenuation will restrict the functionally active band.</p>
<p data-start="3540" data-end="3591">\subsection{Completeness of the Resonant Expansion}</p>
<p data-start="3593" data-end="3666">Combining (\ref{eq:Modal}) with Parseval's identity yields the following.</p>
<p data-start="3668" data-end="3794">\begin{theorem}<br>
