<p data-start="3961" data-end="4127">and the sum converges in $L^2(M)$. If $w_0$ and $w_1$ lie in $H^k(M)$ for any $k\ge 0$, then the convergence holds in $H^k(M)$ for all $t\in\mathbb{R}$.<br>
\end{theorem}</p>
<p data-start="4129" data-end="4448">This establishes that stationary eigenmodes form the natural harmonic building blocks for any spatiotemporal cortical field satisfying a second-order equation of motion. In forthcoming sections, these modes will play the role of the underlying cymatic resonance patterns that govern long-range cortical synchronization.</p>
<p data-start="4450" data-end="4507">\subsection{Biophysical Interpretation of Resonant Modes}</p>
<p data-start="4509" data-end="4869">Equation (\ref{eq:Standing}) admits an interpretation as a standing-wave pattern whose spatial form matches the eigenfunction $u_m$ and whose temporal oscillation is governed by $\omega_m=\sqrt{\lambda_m}$. High-frequency neural oscillations arise from high-$m$ modes, though damping, dispersion, and nonlinearities attenuate higher modes in biological tissue.</p>
<p data-start="4871" data-end="5224">Empirical studies employing ultrafast imaging have observed patterns consistent with spatial eigenmodes of $\Delta$ on the cortical sheet, suggesting that the manifold’s geometry constrains functional connectivity by imposing a discrete set of resonant patterns. These resonant modes furnish the skeleton upon which nonlinear RSVP dynamics will operate.</p>
<p data-start="5226" data-end="5287">\subsection{Spectral Bandwidth and Physiological Constraints}</p>
<p data-start="5289" data-end="5684">Although the spectral decomposition includes arbitrarily high eigenvalues, only a finite band of modes is expected to be physiologically relevant due to synaptic filtering, membrane capacitance, axonal delays, and metabolic constraints. Let $m_{\max}$ be the highest mode index that survives biophysical attenuation. Then the effective functional resonance is governed by the truncated expansion</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≈</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo></msub></munderover><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\mathbf{r},t)\approx \sum_{m=0}^{m_{\max}} c_m(t) u_m(\mathbf{r}).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf">r</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.9296em; vertical-align: -1.2671em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.6625em;"><span style="top: -1.8829em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span><span class="mrel mtight">=</span><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">∑</span></span></span><span style="top: -4.3111em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1645em;"><span style="top: -2.357em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mop mtight"><span class="mtight">m</span><span class="mtight">a</span><span class="mtight">x</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.143em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.2671em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf">r</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="5761" data-end="5913">Determining $m_{\max}$ from experimental data is a crucial problem in practical inference and will be discussed in the section on empirical predictions.</p>
