<p data-start="419" data-end="468">\section{Cymatic Resonance on the Cortical Sheet}</p>
<p data-start="470" data-end="519">\subsection{Driven Dynamics and Resonant Forcing}</p>
<p data-start="521" data-end="972">Let $(M,g)$ be the cortical manifold and let ${u_m}_{m=0}^{\infty}$ denote the complete set of Neumann eigenfunctions of the Laplace--Beltrami operator. Consider a spatiotemporal field $W(\mathbf{r},t)$ driven by an external forcing term $F(\mathbf{r},t)$:<br>
\begin{equation}<br>
\partial_t^2 W - \Delta W = F(\mathbf{r},t),<br>
\label{eq:DrivenWave}<br>
\end{equation}<br>
with $\partial W/\partial n=0$ on $\partial M$. Expanding $W$ and $F$ into modal coordinates,</p>
