-role="assistant" data-message-id="985063ad-9982-4a51-9685-610bd05ac62f" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="536">Below continues the manuscript with <strong data-start="36" data-end="50">Section 14</strong>, written entirely in LaTeX, fully rigorous, academic, and continuous with the previous sections. This section constructs the mathematical coupling between the global eigenmode architecture of the cortical manifold and the local nonlinear transformations (amplistwistors) arising within the RSVP–TARTAN framework. The interplay between locality and global resonance is formalized through modal decompositions, nonlinear operator bounds, stability theorems, and synchronization criteria.</p>
<hr data-start="538" data-end="541">
<p data-start="543" data-end="592">\section{Coupling Eigenmodes with Amplistwistors}</p>
<p data-start="594" data-end="653">\subsection{Local--Global Decomposition of Cortical Fields}</p>
<p data-start="655" data-end="1068">Let $\Psi(\mathbf{r},t)$ denote a general RSVP field on the cortical manifold, representing the collective state of coupled scalar, vector, and entropy components. Assume $\Psi(\cdot,t)\in H^1(M)$ for each $t$, and decompose it into eigenmodes of the Neumann Laplacian:<br>
\begin{equation}<br>
\Psi(\mathbf{r},t) = \sum_{m=0}^{\infty} a_m(t) u_m(\mathbf{r}).<br>
\label{eq:PsiModal}<br>
\end{equation}<br>
The modal coefficients are</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_m(t) = \int_M \Psi(\mathbf{r},t) u_m(\mathbf{r})\, \mathrm{d}\mu_g.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.2719em; vertical-align: -0.9119em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop op-symbol large-op" style="margin-right: 0.44445em; position: relative; top: -0.0011em;">∫</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist"><span style="top: -1.7881em; margin-left: -0.4445em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9119em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf">r</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf">r</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathrm">d</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">μ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">g</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1146" data-end="1230">Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a local nonlinear operator acting pointwise or quasi-pointwise:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{A}\Psi)(\mathbf{r},t) = F(\Psi(\mathbf{r},t)),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal">A</span><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf">r</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf">r</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">))</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1294" data-end="1437">where $F:\mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}^d$ is smooth and satisfies appropriate growth bounds. In the context of amplistwistors, $F$ is of the form</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.2em" maxsize="1.2em">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.2em" maxsize="1.2em">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)=\pi\big(\alpha(x)\,\tau(x) x \big),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.2em; vertical-align: -0.35em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mord"><span class="delimsizing size1">(</span></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mord"><span class="delimsizing size1">)</span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1485" data-end="1674">where $\alpha:\mathbb{R}^d\to\mathbb{R}^+$, $\tau:\mathbb{R}^d\to SO(d)$, and $\pi:\mathbb{R}^d\to\mathbb{R}^d$ is a projection. We assume $F$ is locally Lipschitz and polynomially bounded.</p>
<p data-start="1676" data-end="1918">Our goal is to express $\mathcal{A}\Psi$ in modal coordinates. Projecting onto $u_m$ yields coefficients<br>
\begin{equation}<br>
(\mathcal{A}\Psi)_m(t)=\int_M F(\Psi(\mathbf{r},t)),u_m(\mathbf{r}) ,\mathrm{d}\mu_g.<br>
\label{eq:ModalA}<br>
\end{equation}</p>
<p data-start="1920" data-end="2143">Although $F$ is local, its effect on the modal expansion is global due to the integral against $u_m$. The structure of these integrals governs how local nonlinear amplistwistor dynamics couple to global resonant eigenmodes.</p>
<p data-start="2145" data-end="2200">\subsection{Interaction Coefficients and Mode Coupling}</p>
<p data-start="2202" data-end="2247">Expanding $F(\Psi)$ in a Taylor series yields</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>⋯</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\Psi)=F(0)+DF(0)\Psi + \frac12 D^2F(0)[\Psi,\Psi] + \cdots.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0074em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3214em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="mclose">]</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.313em;"></span><span class="minner">⋯</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2316" data-end="2477">Inserting the modal decomposition (\ref{eq:PsiModal}), we obtain multilinear expressions of the form<br>
\begin{equation}<br>
(\mathcal{A}\Psi)<em data-start="2451" data-end="2463">m(t)= \sum</em>{j} L_{mj} a_j</p>
<ul data-start="2478" data-end="2647">
<li data-start="2478" data-end="2647">
<p data-start="2480" data-end="2647">\sum_{j,k} Q_{mjk} a_j a_k + \sum_{j,k,\ell} C_{mjk\ell} a_j a_k a_\ell + \cdots.<br>
\label{eq:ModalSeries}<br>
\end{equation}<br>
The coefficients are given by integrals such as</p>
</li>
</ul>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{mj} = \int_M (DF(0)u_j) u_m\,\mathrm{d}\mu_g,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">mj</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.2719em; vertical-align: -0.9119em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop op-symbol large-op" style="margin-right: 0.44445em; position: relative; top: -0.0011em;">∫</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist"><span style="top: -1.7881em; margin-left: -0.4445em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9119em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathrm">d</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">μ</span><span class="msupsub"><span clas