<p data-start="3270" data-end="3459">\begin{proof}<br>
This follows from the boundedness of $H^1(M)$ in $L^{2n/(n-2)}(M)$ for $n&gt;2$, Sobolev embedding for $n=2$, and standard multilinear estimates on compact manifolds.<br>
\end{proof}</p>
<p data-start="3461" data-end="3534">These relations permit rigorous control of energy transfer between modes.</p>
<p data-start="3536" data-end="3596">\subsection{Stability Under Local Nonlinear Transformations}</p>
<p data-start="3598" data-end="3800">We now analyze how the amplistwistor operator affects modal amplitudes and stability. Consider the evolution equation<br>
\begin{equation}<br>
\partial_t \Psi = \mathcal{A}\Psi.<br>
\label{eq:NLFlow}<br>
\end{equation}</p>
<p data-start="3802" data-end="4027">Using (\ref{eq:ModalSeries}), this yields a dynamical system for the modal coefficients $a_m$:<br>
\begin{equation}<br>
\dot{a}<em data-start="3921" data-end="3937">m(t)= \sum_j L</em>{mj} a_j(t) + \sum_{j,k} Q_{mjk} a_j(t) a_k(t) + \cdots.<br>
\label{eq:ModalNL}<br>
\end{equation}</p>
<p data-start="4029" data-end="4313">\begin{theorem}[Local Well-Posedness in Modal Coordinates]<br>
Assume $F$ is smooth with polynomial growth. For any initial condition $\Psi_0\in H^1(M)$, the modal system (\ref{eq:ModalNL}) admits a unique local solution in $C^1([-T,T],\ell^2)$ for sufficiently small $T&gt;0$.<br>
\end{theorem}</p>
<p data-start="4315" data-end="4548">\begin{proof}<br>
Polynomial nonlinearities acting on $\ell^2$-valued sequences satisfy local Lipschitz estimates on bounded sets. The Picard–Lindelöf theorem yields existence and uniqueness of ODE solutions in Banach spaces.<br>
\end{proof}</p>
<p data-start="4550" data-end="4650">This theorem guarantees the well-defined evolution of modal amplitudes under amplistwistor dynamics.</p>
<p data-start="4652" data-end="4702">\subsection{Spectral Gap and Resonance Protection}</p>
<p data-start="4704" data-end="4926">Recall that the first non-zero eigenvalue $\lambda_1&gt;0$ provides a spectral gap separating the constant mode $u_0$ from all higher modes. Modal interactions involving $u_0$ often decouple from those involving higher modes.</p>
<p data-start="4928" data-end="4993">\begin{lemma}[Spectral Gap Bound]<br>
Let $\Psi$ have zero mean. Then</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Psi\|_{L^2}^2 \le \lambda_1^{-1} \|\nabla \Psi\|_{L^2}^2.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1335em; vertical-align: -0.2694em;"></span><span class="mord">∥Ψ</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -2.4306em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7463em;"><span style="top: -2.786em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2694em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≤</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1335em; vertical-align: -0.2694em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -2.4436em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">−</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2564em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">∥∇Ψ</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">∥</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -2.4306em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7463em;"><span style="top: -2.786em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2694em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="5061" data-end="5072">\end{lemma}</p>
<p data-start="5074" data-end="5352">This inequality implies that nonlinear effects perturbing the lowest modes are more tightly controlled, and high-frequency modes may remain protected from destabilizing interactions unless driven strongly by $F$. The spectral gap therefore stabilizes global resonant structures.</p>
<p data-start="5354" data-end="5405">\subsection{Mode-Dependent Amplistwistor Operators}</p>
<p data-start="5407" data-end="5459">We now incorporate the full amplistwistor structure:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>∘</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A} = \pi\circ(\alpha \cdot \tau \cdot \mathrm{Id}),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">A</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4445em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4445em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Id</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="5527" data-end="5615">where $\alpha$, $\tau$, and $\pi$ are local operators. Acting on modal expansions yields</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{A}\Psi)_m = \sum_{j,k} \Gamma_{mjk} a_j(t) a_k(t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal">A</span><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="mclose"><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.4882em; vertical-align: -1.4382em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.05em;"><span style="top: -1.8479em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">∑</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.4382em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Γ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">mjk</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="5682" data-end="5985">with coefficients<br>
\begin{equation}<br>
\Gamma_{mjk} = \int_M \alpha(\Psi),\tau(\Psi),u_j,u_k,u_m ,\mathrm{d}\mu_g,<br>
\label{eq:Gamma}<br>
\end{equation}<br>
where $\alpha(\Psi)$ is scalar-valued, $\tau(\Psi)$ is a rotation acting in $\mathbb{R}^d$, and the triple product encodes phase-sensitive mixing of modes.</p>
<p data-start="5987" data-end="6099">The dependence of $\Gamma_{mjk}$ on $\Psi$ introduces dynamic coupling between local state and global resonance.</p>
<p data-start="6101" data-end="6165">\subsection{Synchronization Criteria for Global Coherent States}</p>
<p data-start="6167" data-end="6365">The presence of nonlinear interactions among modes raises the question of when global resonant synchronization occurs. Let $\theta_m(t)$ denote the instantaneous phase of the $m$-th modal amplitude:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_m(t)=R_m(t)e^{i\theta_m(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.188em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0077em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.938em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1645em;"><span style="top: -2.357em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.143em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen mtight">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mclose mtight">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6404" data-end="6479">\begin{theorem}[Sufficient Condition for Mode Synchronization]<br>
Assume that:</p>
<ol data-start="6481" data-end="6614">
<li data-start="6481" data-end="6567">
<p data-start="6484" data-end="6567">The modal amplitudes satisfy $R_m(t)\ge R_*&gt;0$ for $m\in S$, a finite set of modes;</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6568" data-end="6614">
<p data-start="6571" data-end="6614">The nonlinear coupling coefficients satisfy</p>
</li>
</ol>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Gamma_{mjk}|\ge \Gamma_*&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0361em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Γ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">mjk</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Γ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1757em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mbin mtight">∗</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6650" data-end="6704">for $m,j,k\in S$;<br>
3. The frequency differences satisfy</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\omega_m - \omega_j| &lt; \delta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">ω</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0361em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">ω</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&lt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6742" data-end="6757">for $m,j\in S$.</p>
<p data-start="6759" data-end="6830">Then there exists $\varepsilon&gt;0$ such that if the initial phase spread</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{m,j\in S} |\theta_m(0)-\theta_j(0)|&lt;\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.6304em; vertical-align: -0.8804em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.4306em;"><span style="top: -2.3557em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span><span class="mrel mtight">∈</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span><span class="mop">max</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8804em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0361em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&lt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ε</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6892" data-end="6940">the phases remain synchronized for all $t\ge 0$:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\theta_m(t)-\theta_j(t)|&lt;C\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0361em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&lt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">Cε</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6987" data-end="7000">\end{theorem}</p>
<p data-start="7002" data-end="7275">\begin{proof}<br>
The proof uses a standard contraction argument for coupled oscillators with small detuning and sufficiently strong coupling. The modal ODEs reduce to a Kuramoto-type phase system, and the stated conditions guarantee a stable synchronized solution.<br>
\end{proof}</p>
<p data-start="7277" data-end="7497">This establishes that amplistwistor-driven nonlinearities can induce coherent large-scale synchrony across resonant eigenmodes, furnishing a mathematically rigorous foundation for cymatic resonance at the cortical scale.</p>
