<p data-start="3472" data-end="3549">which manifest as canonical phase-amplitude coupling effects.<br>
\end{enumerate}</p>
<p data-start="3551" data-end="3706">These relationships can be tested by fitting modal phases to high-density MEG recordings using cortical meshes derived from individual MRI reconstructions.</p>
<p data-start="3708" data-end="3762">\subsection{Predicted Effects of External Stimulation}</p>
<p data-start="3764" data-end="3990">External stimulation---magnetic, electrical, or rhythmic sensory---acts as a forcing term in (\ref{eq:DrivenWave}). If a stimulation source has spatial profile $h(\mathbf{r})$ and temporal frequency $\nu$, the modal forcing is</p>
