<p data-start="5930" data-end="5987">\subsection{Predictions for Language Processing Dynamics}</p>
<p data-start="5989" data-end="6165">The RSVP field equations introduce nonlinear interactions among scalar, vector, and entropy fields. Their modal projections inherit the resonant structure above. In particular:</p>
<p data-start="6167" data-end="6877">\begin{enumerate}<br>
\item The temporal progression observed in cortical language areas corresponds to transitions across resonant modes: early sensory processing activates low-index modes; deeper semantic processing recruits mid-range modes; integrative or narrative-level processing activates the lowest-frequency spatially global modes.<br>
\item High-level interpretational dynamics (e.g., integration across sentences) require sustained activity in the smallest eigenmodes, with time horizons proportional to $\omega_m^{-1}$.<br>
\item Prediction errors modulate entropy $S$, perturbing the effective Laplacian and producing spectral broadening; this effect is reduced in highly predictable contexts.<br>
\end{enumerate}</p>
<p data-start="6879" data-end="6977">These predictions directly link empirical neuroscientific findings to geometric properties of $M$.</p>
<p data-start="6979" data-end="7037">\subsection{Statistical Tests for Eigenmode Decomposition}</p>
