"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="449">Below continues the manuscript with <strong data-start="36" data-end="50">Section 16</strong>, written entirely in LaTeX, maintaining academic rigor and internal consistency with all prior sections. This is one of the central sections of the treatise: the <em data-start="213" data-end="306">full coupling of the RSVP field equations to the spectral geometry of the cortical manifold</em>, establishing the governing PDE in modal coordinates, nonlinear energy estimates, and resonance structures induced by amplistwistor recursion.</p>
<hr data-start="451" data-end="454">
<p data-start="456" data-end="509">\section{Coupling RSVP Dynamics to Spectral Geometry}</p>
<p data-start="511" data-end="569">\subsection{RSVP Field Equations on a Riemannian Manifold}</p>
<p data-start="571" data-end="702">Recall that the RSVP framework models cognitive dynamics through three interacting fields defined on the cortical manifold $(M,g)$:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(scalar&nbsp;potential)</mtext><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\mathbf{r},t) \quad \text{(scalar potential)},</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf">r</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">(scalar&nbsp;potential)</span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(vector&nbsp;flow&nbsp;field)</mtext><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{r},t) \quad \text{(vector flow field)},</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf">r</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">(vector&nbsp;flow&nbsp;field)</span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(entropy/uncertainty&nbsp;field)</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(\mathbf{r},t) \quad \text{(entropy/uncertainty field)}.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf">r</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">(entropy/uncertainty&nbsp;field)</span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="892" data-end="944">The general form of the RSVP system is expressed as:</p>
<p data-start="946" data-end="1318">\begin{equation}<br>
\begin{aligned}<br>
\partial_t \Phi &amp;= c_1 \Delta \Phi + c_2,(\Phi \times \mathbf{v}) - c_3 S\Phi + \eta_\Phi, \<br>
\partial_t \mathbf{v} &amp;= c_4 \nabla \Phi + c_5,\nabla \times \mathbf{v} - c_6 S\mathbf{v} + \eta_{\mathbf{v}}, \<br>
\partial_t S &amp;= c_7 |\nabla \cdot \mathbf{v}| + c_8 \Phi^2 - c_9 S + \eta_{S},<br>
\end{aligned}<br>
\label{eq:RSVPsystem}<br>
\end{equation}</p>
<p data-start="1320" data-end="1529">with Neumann boundary conditions imposed on all components. Here $\eta_\Phi$, $\eta_{\mathbf{v}}$, and $\eta_{S}$ are noise processes satisfying standard martingale bounds and admissible covariance structures.</p>
<p data-start="1531" data-end="1731">Our task is now to reformulate these coupled PDEs in the eigenbasis of the Laplace–Beltrami operator and understand how their nonlinear interactions produce resonance phenomena and recursive dynamics.</p>
<p data-start="1733" data-end="1784">\subsection{Modal Decomposition of the RSVP Fields}</p>
<p data-start="1786" data-end="1832">Expand each field into the Neumann eigenbasis:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(\mathbf{r},t) = \sum_{m=0}^\infty \phi_m(t) u_m(\mathbf{r}),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf">r</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.9185em; vertical-align: -1.2671em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.6514em;"><span style="top: -1.8829em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span><span class="mrel mtight">=</span><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol l