<p data-start="3900" data-end="4056">Standard elliptic estimates guarantee that these integrals decay sufficiently fast as $j,k\to\infty$ to ensure local well-posedness of the modal ODE system.</p>
<p data-start="4058" data-end="4108">\subsection{Full Modal Form of the RSVP Equations}</p>
<p data-start="4110" data-end="4191">The complete PDE system reduces to the following infinite-dimensional ODE system:</p>
<p data-start="4193" data-end="4250">\begin{equation}<br>
\partial_t \phi_m = -c_1\lambda_m \phi_m</p>
<ul data-start="4251" data-end="4324">
<li data-start="4251" data-end="4324">
<p data-start="4253" data-end="4324">c_2 \sum_{j,k} N^{(\Phi\times\mathbf{v})}_{m,j,k},\phi_j,\mathbf{v}_k</p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul data-start="4325" data-end="4376">
<li data-start="4325" data-end="4376">
<p data-start="4327" data-end="4376">c_3 \sum_{j,k} N^{(\Phi S)}_{m,j,k},\phi_j,s_k</p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul data-start="4377" data-end="4428">
<li data-start="4377" data-end="4428">
<p data-start="4379" data-end="4428">\eta_{\Phi,m},<br>
\label{eq:phiModal}<br>
\end{equation}</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4430" data-end="4499">\begin{equation}<br>
\partial_t \mathbf{v}_m = -c_5\lambda_m \mathbf{v}_m</p>
<ul data-start="4500" data-end="4543">
<li data-start="4500" data-end="4543">
<p data-start="4502" data-end="4543">c_4 \sum_j M^{(\nabla\Phi)}_{m,j},\phi_j</p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul data-start="4544" data-end="4601">
<li data-start="4544" data-end="4601">
<p data-start="4546" data-end="4601">c_6 \sum_k N^{(\mathbf{v}S)}_{m,j,k},\mathbf{v}_j,s_k</p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul data-start="4602" data-end="4657">
<li data-start="4602" data-end="4657">
<p data-start="4604" data-end="4657">\eta_{\mathbf{v},m},<br>
\label{eq:vModal}<br>
\end{equation}</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4659" data-end="4701">\begin{equation}<br>
\partial_t s_m = -c_9 s_m</p>
<ul data-start="4702" data-end="4885">
<li data-start="4702" data-end="4785">
<p data-start="4704" data-end="4785">c_7 \sum_{j,k} C_{m,j,k}^{(\nabla\cdot\mathbf{v})},\mathbf{v}_j\cdot\mathbf{v}_k</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4786" data-end="4838">
<p data-start="4788" data-end="4838">c_8 \sum_{j,k} N^{(\Phi^2)}_{m,j,k},\phi_j \phi_k</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4839" data-end="4885">
<p data-start="4841" data-end="4885">\eta_{S,m}.<br>
\label{eq:SModal}<br>
\end{equation}</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4887" data-end="5094">Each triplet of indices $(m,j,k)$ acts as a nonlinear coupling site among three spectral modes. The structure is analogous to nonlinear wave equations, quantum turbulence, and mode-coupled oscillatory media.</p>
<p data-start="5096" data-end="5146">\subsection{Energy Estimates and Global Existence}</p>
