ce" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∼</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.4882em; vertical-align: -1.4382em;"></span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.05em;"><span style="top: -1.8479em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">∑</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.4382em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">mjk</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">s</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">ϕ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="7323" data-end="7471">\begin{lemma}[Entropy-Mediated Mode Suppression]<br>
If $s_k$ grows sufficiently large, then for all $j$ interacting with $k$ through nonzero $N_{mjk}$,</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_t |\phi_j| &lt; 0.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0361em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">∂</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0556em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">ϕ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&lt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="7503" data-end="7514">\end{lemma}</p>
<p data-start="7516" data-end="7568">This defines a mathematically precise mechanism for:</p>
<ol data-start="7570" data-end="7727">
<li data-start="7570" data-end="7617">
<p data-start="7573" data-end="7617">inhibiting irrelevant semantic hypotheses,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7618" data-end="7662">
<p data-start="7621" data-end="7662">suppressing noise-induced oscillations,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7663" data-end="7727">
<p data-start="7666" data-end="7727">sharpening resonant ensembles into coherent cognitive states.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="7729" data-end="7808">This mirrors the role of inhibition and gain control in cortical microcircuits.</p>
<p data-start="7811" data-end="7883">\subsection{Bifurcation Cascades and Recursive Deepening of Time Scales}</p>
<p data-start="7885" data-end="7984">Iterative bifurcation analysis reveals that recursive amplification structures appear sequentially:</p>
<p data-start="7986" data-end="8269">\begin{enumerate}<br>
\item At first bifurcation: dominant large-scale mode oscillation emerges.<br data-start="8078" data-end="8081">
\item At second bifurcation: quadratic interactions activate mid-scale modes.<br data-start="8158" data-end="8161">
\item At third bifurcation: fine-scale modes entrain, producing cross-frequency structure.<br data-start="8251" data-end="8254">
\end{enumerate}</p>
<p data-start="8271" data-end="8361">This mathematically reproduces the empirical temporal hierarchy in language comprehension:</p>
<p data-start="8363" data-end="8629">\begin{itemize}<br>
\item 50–100 ms: phonological and early sensory processing,<br data-start="8438" data-end="8441">
\item 200–300 ms: lexical and syntactic evaluation (N400/P600),<br data-start="8504" data-end="8507">
\item 400–600 ms: phrase and narrative integration,<br data-start="8558" data-end="8561">
\item 1–2 s: discourse-level coherence and prediction.<br>
\end{itemize}</p>
<p data-start="8631" data-end="8731">Each tier corresponds to a deeper level of the resonant–recursive cascade in the RSVP–TARTAN system.</p>
<p data-start="8734" data-end="8768">\subsection{Summary of Section 18}</p>
<p data-start="8770" data-end="8835">This section has provided a rigorous mathematical foundation for:</p>
<p data-start="8837" data-end="9272">\begin{enumerate}<br>
\item nonlinear stability and destabilization of resonant eigenmodes;<br data-start="8924" data-end="8927">
\item Hopf bifurcations generating oscillatory semantic cycles;<br data-start="8990" data-end="8993">
\item nonlinear mixing producing cross-frequency coupling;<br data-start="9051" data-end="9054">
\item selective activation of modes determined by geometric damping;<br data-start="9122" data-end="9125">
\item entropy-driven suppression of irrelevant modes;<br data-start="9178" data-end="9181">
\item bifurcation cascades creating a hierarchical temporal architecture.<br data-start="9254" data-end="9257">
\end{enumerate}</p>
<p data-start="9274" data-end="9553">These phenomena collectively demonstrate how the RSVP–TARTAN system naturally produces multilayered, transformer-like sequence processing without assuming discrete layers. Instead, layers emerge dynamically from spectral geometry, nonlinear interactions, and recursive resonance.</p>
