<p data-start="4181" data-end="4192">\end{lemma}</p>
<p data-start="4194" data-end="4324">\begin{proof}<br>
The $H^1$ norm squares to $\sum_m \lambda_m |a_m|^2$, and expected amplitude decays as $\lambda_m^{-1}$.<br>
\end{proof}</p>
<p data-start="4326" data-end="4423">Thus the system naturally preserves sufficient regularity for interpretation as a cortical field.</p>
<p data-start="4426" data-end="4484">\subsection{Wong–Zakai Approximation and Neural Filtering}</p>
<p data-start="4486" data-end="4723">The reconstructed fMRI and ECoG signals represent temporally filtered versions of underlying dynamics. Wong–Zakai theory provides a rigorous framework: smooth approximations of Wiener noise converge to Stratonovich solutions of the SPDE.</p>
<p data-start="4725" data-end="4867">\begin{theorem}[Wong–Zakai Approximation]<br>
Let $W^\epsilon(t)$ be a sequence of smooth approximations to the Wiener process. Then the solutions</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\Psi^\epsilon
= [ -A\Psi^\epsilon + F(\Psi^\epsilon) ]\,\mathrm{d}t
+ G\, \mathrm{d}W^\epsilon(t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7144em;"></span><span class="mord mathrm">d</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7144em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">ϵ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7144em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">ϵ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7144em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">ϵ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)]</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathrm">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathrm">d</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">W</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7144em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">ϵ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4982" data-end="5073">converge in probability to the Stratonovich solution of the RSVP–TARTAN SPDE.<br>
\end{theorem}</p>
<p data-start="5075" data-end="5231">This justifies interpreting measured signals as smoothed versions of RSVP dynamics, with neural filtering effectively implementing Stratonovich integration.</p>
<p data-start="5234" data-end="5299">\subsection{Stochastic Resonance: Noise Enhances Mode Activation}</p>
<p data-start="5301" data-end="5434">Noise does not merely perturb dynamics; it can amplify specific eigenmodes by coherently injecting energy near resonance frequencies.</p>
<p data-start="5436" data-end="5459">Consider a single mode:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d} a_m(t)
= -\lambda_m a_m(t)\,\mathrm{d}t
+ \mathrm{d}W_m(t).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathrm">d</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.