<p data-start="6225" data-end="6445">\begin{proof}<br>
Standard analysis of a stochastically forced linear oscillator using Fourier transform methods. The transfer function peaks near resonance, with additive contribution from stochastic excitation.<br>
\end{proof}</p>
<p data-start="6447" data-end="6492">This provides a quantitative explanation for:</p>
<ol data-start="6494" data-end="6684">
<li data-start="6494" data-end="6556">
<p data-start="6497" data-end="6556">enhanced low-frequency oscillations under moderate noise,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6557" data-end="6615">
<p data-start="6560" data-end="6615">noise-facilitated binding during semantic processing,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6616" data-end="6684">
<p data-start="6619" data-end="6684">experimentally observed stochastic resonance in cortical systems.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="6687" data-end="6748">\subsection{Noise-Driven Transitions Between Resonant States}</p>
