<p data-start="1454" data-end="1943">with $f_m$ capturing the intrinsic nonlinear interactions and $g_m$ representing higher-frequency modulations, stochastic influences, or recursive corrections arising from TARTAN tiling. The small parameter $\epsilon$ may represent the ratio of fast to slow timescales, the strength of noise, or the magnitude of higher harmonic components. Such a representation suggests the introduction of a fast timescale $\tau = t/\epsilon$ and a slow timescale $T = t$, leading to the extended system</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∂</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∂</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∂</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∂</mi><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial a_m}{\partial T} + \frac{1}{\epsilon}\frac{\partial a_m}{\partial \tau}
