<p data-start="196" data-end="269">\section{Phase Geometry and the Synchronization of Distributed Inference}</p>
<p data-start="271" data-end="1029">The recursive field dynamics developed thus far operate within a geometric and energetic substrate whose temporal structure is not uniform but stratified across multiple oscillatory regimes. The synchronization of distributed inference therefore requires a precise account of how phase relationships develop across the resonant manifold and how they constrain the evolution of the tri-field system. The present section introduces the notion of phase geometry, formalizing oscillatory phase as a geometric parameter that modulates both local amplistwistor actions and global correction flows. This treatment unifies the behaviour of the RSVP fields with empirical observations of phase coupling and phase-dependent stimulus sensitivity in cortical recordings.</p>
