<h3 data-start="849" data-end="872"><strong data-start="853" data-end="872">1. Introduction</strong></h3>
<h3 data-start="874" data-end="918"><strong data-start="878" data-end="918">2. Neuroscience of Cortical Dynamics</strong></h3>
<p data-start="919" data-end="1016">Cortical columns, oscillations, multi-scale temporal integration, empirical language hierarchies.</p>
<h3 data-start="1018" data-end="1060"><strong data-start="1022" data-end="1060">3. Spectral Geometry of the Cortex</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1061" data-end="1169">Riemannian cortical surface, Laplace–Beltrami operator, eigenfunctions, Weyl scaling, geometric constraints.</p>
<h3 data-start="1171" data-end="1228"><strong data-start="1175" data-end="1228">4. RSVP Theory: Formal Mathematical Specification</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1229" data-end="1309">Scalar–vector–entropy fields, relativistic invariants, dynamical coupling terms.</p>
<h3 data-start="1311" data-end="1351"><strong data-start="1315" data-end="1351">5. The TARTAN Recursion Operator</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1352" data-end="1428">Formal definition, recursion on fields, multi-scale tiling, annotated noise.</p>
<h3 data-start="1430" data-end="1481"><strong data-start="1434" data-end="1481">6. Amplistwistors: Complex-Analytic Origins</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1482" data-end="1585">Generalization of Needham’s amplitwist, amplitude–twist–projection operators, nonlinear local dynamics.</p>
<h3 data-start="1587" data-end="1650"><strong data-start="1591" data-end="1650">7. Cortical Columns as Cascaded Amplistwistor Operators</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1651" data-end="1736">Biophysical interpretation, microcircuit constraints, recurrent microcolumn dynamics.</p>
<h3 data-start="1738" data-end="1785"><strong data-start="1742" data-end="1785">8. Continuous Dynamics: PDE Formulation</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1786" data-end="1899">Derivation of PDEs governing field evolution, curved manifold generalization, boundary and regularity conditions.</p>
<h3 data-start="1901" data-end="1970"><strong data-start="1905" data-end="1970">9. Functional Analytic Results: Semigroups and Well-Posedness</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1971" data-end="2070">Sectorial operators, Hille–Yosida, smoothing properties, existence and uniqueness, noise structure.</p>
<h3 data-start="2072" data-end="2138"><strong data-start="2076" data-end="2138">10. Universal Approximation via Amplistwistor Compositions</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2139" data-end="2227">Generalization of Cybenko/Hornik/Poggio for manifold-valued fields; constructive bounds.</p>
<h3 data-start="2229" data-end="2286"><strong data-start="2233" data-end="2286">11. Spectral Decomposition and Eigenmode Dynamics</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2287" data-end="2382">Modal decomposition, energy transfer, traveling versus standing waves, nonlinear mode coupling.</p>
<h3 data-start="2384" data-end="2440"><strong data-start="2388" data-end="2440">12. Alignment With Cortical Language Hierarchies</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2441" data-end="2580">Direct comparison with Goldstein et al. (2025): LLM-layer → temporal latency mapping, temporal receptive windows, recursive semantic depth.</p>
<h3 data-start="2582" data-end="2630"><strong data-start="2586" data-end="2630">13. Empirical Evidence (ECoG, MEG, fMRI)</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2631" data-end="2896">14.1 ECoG evidence for temporal hierarchies<br data-start="2674" data-end="2677">
