<p data-start="2151" data-end="2200">Semigroup generation by the linearized operator</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2201" data-end="2240">
<p data-start="2203" data-end="2240">Regularity and smoothing properties</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2242" data-end="2289">Reviewers <em data-start="2252" data-end="2258">will</em> ask for this if it is omitted.</p>
<hr data-start="2291" data-end="2294">
<h2 data-start="2296" data-end="2365"><strong data-start="2299" data-end="2365">Appendix C: Universal Approximation via Amplistwistor Cascades</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2366" data-end="2389">This appendix includes:</p>
<ul data-start="2391" data-end="2606">
<li data-start="2391" data-end="2455">
<p data-start="2393" data-end="2455">The full Stone–Weierstrass argument for Banach-valued fields</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2456" data-end="2519">
<p data-start="2458" data-end="2519">Proof that amplistwistors form an algebra separating points</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2520" data-end="2543">
<p data-start="2522" data-end="2543">Approximation rates</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2544" data-end="2564">
<p data-start="2546" data-end="2564">Example cascades</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2565" data-end="2606">
<p data-start="2567" data-end="2606">Dimension-dependent complexity bounds</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2608" data-end="2731">These proofs are too long for the main text and clutter the argument, but they are crucial to the theoretical contribution.</p>
<hr data-start="2733" data-end="2736">
<h2 data-start="2738" data-end="2797"><strong data-start="2741" data-end="2797">Appendix D: Spectral Geometry and Eigenmode Analysis</strong></h2>
