    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"## 2. Synthetic LLM Layer Embeddings\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"For each word and each layer, we sample a random vector in a low-dimensional\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"space (e.g. 32 dimensions). In real experiments, these would be contextual\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"embeddings extracted from each layer of a transformer model like GPT-2 XL.\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Here, we treat them as random features with a smooth \"depth\" structure so that\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"deeper layers carry increasingly abstract information over longer time scales."</span></span><span>
