   </span><span><span class="hljs-attr">"source"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">[</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"## 3. Temporal Kernels for Cortical Regions\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"We define four regions, each with a characteristic temporal kernel:\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"- **mSTG**: early, narrow window (phonetic/early acoustic).\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"- **aSTG**: intermediate window (syntactic/integration).\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"- **IFG**: later, broader window.\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"- **TP**: longest, broadest window (semantic/inferential integration).\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Each kernel is modeled as a normalized Gaussian over lags, with region-specific\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    <span class="hljs-string">"mean and variance. This is a stylized analogue of graded temporal receptive\n,
    "</span>windows along the ventral stream.<span class="hljs-string">"
