   </span><span><span class="hljs-attr">"source"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">[</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"## 8. Temporal Receptive Window Widths\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"For each region, we can also quantify the *width* of the temporal receptive\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"field by examining how sharply tuned correlations are around the best lag.\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"This is a crude analogue of the expansion of temporal windows from mSTG to TP\n"</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"reported empirically, but sufficient to explore qualitative behavior."</span></span><span>
   </span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">]</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">}</span></span><span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span></span><span>
