We now define a one-dimensional amplistwistor transform for temporal regressors.
For each scalar regressor \( x(t) \), we construct:

</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">1.</span></span><span> An amplitude envelope via a smoothed squared signal.
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">2.</span></span><span> A twist implemented as a phase rotation in the Fourier domain.
