<li data-start="15174" data-end="15320">
<p data-start="15176" data-end="15320">Make a small <strong data-start="15189" data-end="15206">helper script</strong> that exports figures from these three notebooks directly into your LaTeX <code data-start="15280" data-end="15290">figures/</code> tree with consistent names.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="15321" data-end="15457" data-is-last-node="">
<p data-start="15323" data-end="15457" data-is-last-node="">Or wire in <strong data-start="15334" data-end="15357">file-based exchange</strong> so notebook 2 saves specific regressors that notebook 3 automatically loads and uses as <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">s</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
