844f-4c8dd3b6651b" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="140">That actually matters a <em data-start="24" data-end="29">lot</em>, because the best structure depends on how visible, modular, and long-lived you expect this project to become.</p>
<p data-start="142" data-end="453">Below is a <strong data-start="153" data-end="171">decision guide</strong> tailored to your ecosystem (RSVP, TARTAN, HYDRA, the alphabet essays, etc.) and your typical workflow (large LaTeX treatises, simulation notebooks, interactive renderings, Blender pipelines, etc.). I’ll also give the recommended folder structure for each option and the trade-offs.</p>
<hr data-start="455" data-end="458">
<h1 data-start="460" data-end="503">🧭 Should this become its own repository?</h1>
<h2 data-start="505" data-end="574"><strong data-start="508" data-end="574">Option A — A dedicated repository: <em data-start="545" data-end="572">“cortical-amplistwistors”</em></strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="575" data-end="594">Recommended if:</h3>
<ul data-start="595" data-end="945">
<li data-start="595" data-end="677">
<p data-start="597" data-end="677">You want this project to stand alone as a <em data-start="639" data-end="676">mathematical neuroscience monograph</em>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="678" data-end="736">
<p data-start="680" data-end="736">You expect to publish the PDF formally or semi-formally.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="737" data-end="782">
<p data-start="739" data-end="782">You want to share or cite it independently.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="783" data-end="868">
<p data-start="785" data-end="868">You foresee adding simulations, figures, notebooks, and code that could grow large.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="869" data-end="945">
<p data-start="871" data-end="945">The PDE + empirical validation + PyTorch simulations form a coherent work.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="947" data-end="960">Benefits:</h3>
<ul data-start="961" data-end="1370">
<li data-start="961" data-end="1047">
<p data-start="963" data-end="1047">Clean boundaries: This project does not get entangled with unrelated RSVP materials.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1048" data-end="1134">
<p data-start="1050" data-end="1134">Easy to point collaborators to: “Here is the cortical columns + amplitwistor paper.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1135" data-end="1370">
<p data-start="1137" data-end="1180">Encourages a curated directory structure:</p>
