<h3 data-start="2217" data-end="2231">Downsides:</h3>
<ul data-start="2232" data-end="2336">
<li data-start="2232" data-end="2269">
<p data-start="2234" data-end="2269">Harder for outside viewers to find.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2270" data-end="2336">
<p data-start="2272" data-end="2336">Notebook paths, relative dirs, and Docker/Makefiles may collide.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2338" data-end="2411"><strong data-start="2338" data-end="2411">This keeps your ecosystem unified, but sacrifices modular visibility.</strong></p>
<hr data-start="2413" data-end="2416">
<h1 data-start="2418" data-end="2478">🔧 Option C — Put it inside <strong data-start="2448" data-end="2460">library/</strong> (not recommended)</h1>
<p data-start="2479" data-end="2566">Your <code data-start="2484" data-end="2493">library</code> repo is usually for general-purpose tools, utilities, or code libraries.</p>
<h3 data-start="2568" data-end="2581">Problems:</h3>
<ul data-start="2582" data-end="2767">
<li data-start="2582" data-end="2650">
<p data-start="2584" data-end="2650">This project is not a utility library; it is a research monograph.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2651" data-end="2708">
<p data-start="2653" data-end="2708">LaTeX + notebooks + PDE experiments don’t belong there.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2709" data-end="2767">
<p data-start="2711" data-end="2767">You'll confuse future-you trying to locate the material.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2769" data-end="2789"><strong data-start="2769" data-end="2789">Not recommended.</strong></p>
<hr data-start="2791" data-end="2794">
<h1 data-start="2796" data-end="2860">🔤 Option D — Put it inside <strong data-start="2826" data-end="2839">alphabet/</strong> (maybe, but fragile)</h1>
<p data-start="2861" data-end="2936">Alphabet is where your conceptual essays and philosophical frameworks live.</p>
<h3 data-start="2938" data-end="2956">Could work if:</h3>
<ul data-start="2957" data-end="3105">
<li data-start="2957" data-end="3105">
<p data-start="2959" data-end="3105">You want “Cortical Columns as Amplitwistor Cascades” to be a metaphorical or conceptual installment—like <strong data-start="3064" data-end="3085">“C is for Cortex”</strong> in your A–Z series.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="3107" data-end="3115">But:</h3>
<ul data-start="3116" data-end="3273">
<li data-start="3116" data-end="3171">
<p data-start="3118" data-end="3171">The document is extremely technical and mathematical.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3172" data-end="3235">
<p data-start="3174" data-end="3235">It does not fit the tone or structure of the alphabet essays.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3236" data-end="3273">
<p data-start="3238" data-end="3273">It’s far too large for that format.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3275" data-end="3338"><strong data-start="3275" data-end="3338">Also not recommended unless reframed as a conceptual essay.</strong></p>
<hr data-start="3340" data-end="3343">
<h1 data-start="3345" data-end="3376">🧠 My Recommendation (Strong)</h1>
<h2 data-start="3378" data-end="3411">➤ <strong data-start="3383" data-end="3409">Make a standalone repo</strong></h2>
