<h2 data-start="3345" data-end="3357">Notebooks</h2>
<p data-start="3359" data-end="3428">The following Jupyter notebooks reproduce all computational elements:</p>
<h3 data-start="3430" data-end="3469">1. <code data-start="3437" data-end="3469">amplistwistor_regressors.ipynb</code></h3>
<p data-start="3470" data-end="3540">Temporal amplitwistor-based transformations of LLM-derived regressors.</p>
<h3 data-start="3542" data-end="3584">2. <code data-start="3549" data-end="3584">cortical_temporal_alignment.ipynb</code></h3>
<p data-start="3585" data-end="3644">Reproduces the layer–lag alignment analyses from ECoG data.</p>
<h3 data-start="3646" data-end="3681">3. <code data-start="3653" data-end="3681">rsvp_pytorch_gpu_sim.ipynb</code></h3>
<p data-start="3682" data-end="3760">A GPU-accelerated PyTorch implementation of RSVP scalar–vector–entropy fields.</p>
<h3 data-start="3762" data-end="3805">4. <code data-start="3769" data-end="3805">amplistwistor_field_dynamics.ipynb</code></h3>
<p data-start="3806" data-end="3877">Local nonlinear field transformations and cascade stability properties.</p>
<p data-start="3879" data-end="3968">All notebooks run on CPU; the PyTorch ones accelerate automatically if CUDA<br>
is available.</p>
