    </span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">a</span></span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-attr">href</span></span><span>=</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"https://github.com/Flyxion/amplistwistor-cascades"</span></span><span>&gt;GitHub Repository</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">a</span></span></span><span>&gt;</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;
    </span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">a</span></span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-attr">href</span></span><span>=</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"notebooks/"</span></span><span>&gt;Interactive Jupyter Notebooks</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">a</span></span></span><span>&gt;</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;
    </span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">a</span></span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-attr">href</span></span><span>=</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"figs/"</span></span><span>&gt;Figures and TikZ Diagrams</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">a</span></span></span><span>&gt;</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">ul</span></span></span><span>&gt;
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span></span></span><span>&gt;

</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span></span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-attr">class</span></span><span>=</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"section"</span></span><span>&gt;
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h2</span></span></span><span>&gt;Summary</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h2</span></span></span><span>&gt;
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span></span></span><span>&gt;
Amplistwistors extend Tristan Needham’s geometric “amplitwist” derivative into
a nonlinear operator suitable for modeling cortical computation. Cascades of
these operators exhibit universal approximation properties analogous to deep
neural networks, while admitting a continuous PDE formulation compatible with
neural field theory (Breakspear, 2017; Deco et al., 2009).
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span></span></span><span>&gt;

</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span></span></span><span>&gt;
Empirical alignment comes from:
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span></span></span><span>&gt;

</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">ul</span></span></span><span>&gt;
    </span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;the layer–time isomorphism in ECoG language responses 
        (Goldstein et al., 2025),</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;
    </span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;standing-wave eigenmodes in cortex revealed by ultrafast fMRI 
        (Cabral, Fernandes &amp; Shemesh, 2023),</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;
    </span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;temporal hierarchy templates predicted by spectral geometry 
        (Roberts et al., 2019),</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;
    </span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;predictive, hierarchical cortical models (Friston et al.),</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;
    </span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;universal approximation theorems (Cybenko 1989; Hornik 1991;  
        Poggio &amp; Girosi 1990),</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;
    </span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;and hierarchical learning results in deep networks 
        (Saxe, McClelland &amp; Ganguli, 2013).</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">li</span></span></span><span>&gt;
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">ul</span></span></span><span>&gt;

</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span></span></span><span>&gt;

