This repository, maintained under the </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**standardgalactic**</span></span><span> GitHub account,
contains the full research monograph, simulation code, notebooks, and
reproducible experiments for the project </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Amplistwistor Cascades**</span></span><span> —
a mathematical and neurocomputational framework modeling cortical columns as
cascades of geometric amplitwistor transformations acting on
relativistic scalar–vector fields.

The project is authored scientifically by </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Flyxion**</span></span><span>, but hosted here for
visibility and integration with the broader </span><span><span class="hljs-emphasis">*standardgalactic*</span></span><span> research
ecosystem.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## Overview</span></span><span>

Amplistwistors generalize Needham’s geometric </span><span><span class="hljs-emphasis">*amplitwist*</span></span><span> into a nonlinear
transformation operator acting on high-dimensional neural fields. A cascade of
these operators models the intra-columnar computational dynamics of cortex, with
connections to:

</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> nonlinear hierarchical transformations in deep networks  
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> universal approximation theorems (Cybenko 1989; Hornik 1991; Poggio–Girosi 1990)  
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> large-scale neural dynamics (Breakspear 2017; Deco et al. 2009)  
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> spectral eigenmodes revealed by ultrafast fMRI (Cabral–Fernandes–Shemesh 2023)  
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> temporal hierarchy in human language processing (Goldstein et al., 2025)

The repository contains both the theoretical manuscript and practical
implementations demonstrating the geometric and analytic structure of these
operations.

---

