</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h3</span></span></span><span>&gt;Geometric Operators for Cortical Computation</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h3</span></span></span><span>&gt;

</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span></span></span><span>&gt;
This site presents the online version of </span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">strong</span></span></span><span>&gt;Amplistwistor Cascades</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">strong</span></span></span><span>&gt;,
a mathematical and computational neuroscience project authored by
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">strong</span></span></span><span>&gt;Flyxion</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">strong</span></span></span><span>&gt; and maintained under the
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">strong</span></span></span><span>&gt;standardgalactic</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">strong</span></span></span><span>&gt; research umbrella.
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span></span></span><span>&gt;

</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span></span></span><span>&gt;
The framework develops a geometric model of cortical computation where
cortical columns act as cascades of amplitwistor transformations acting on
relativistic scalar–vector fields. This captures nonlinear hierarchical
processing, spectral structure, and empirical temporal dynamics observed in
ECoG, fMRI, and MEG studies.
</span><span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span></span></span><span>&gt;

