</li>
<li data-start="1367" data-end="1375">
<p data-start="1369" data-end="1375"><code data-start="1369" data-end="1375">.log</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1376" data-end="1391">
<p data-start="1378" data-end="1391"><code data-start="1378" data-end="1391">.synctex.gz</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1392" data-end="1400">
<p data-start="1394" data-end="1400"><code data-start="1394" data-end="1400">.out</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1401" data-end="1417">
<p data-start="1403" data-end="1417"><code data-start="1403" data-end="1417">.fdb_latexmk</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1418" data-end="1426">
<p data-start="1420" data-end="1426"><code data-start="1420" data-end="1426">.fls</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1428" data-end="1491">Meaning: <strong data-start="1437" data-end="1490">all LaTeX build artifacts stay in version control</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="1493" data-end="1537">For research reproducibility, this is ideal.</p>
<hr data-start="1539" data-end="1542">
<h2 data-start="1544" data-end="1586"><strong data-start="1547" data-end="1584">Option B — No <code data-start="1563" data-end="1575">.gitignore</code> at all</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1587" data-end="1625">Some researchers do this deliberately.</p>
<p data-start="1627" data-end="1632">Pros:</p>
<ul data-start="1633" data-end="1701">
<li data-start="1633" data-end="1673">
<p data-start="1635" data-end="1673">100% of build artifacts are preserved.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1674" data-end="1701">
<p data-start="1676" data-end="1701">Maximum historical trace.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1703" data-end="1708">Cons:</p>
<ul data-start="1709" data-end="1807">
<li data-start="1709" data-end="1759">
<p data-start="1711" data-end="1759">The GitHub repo becomes large much more quickly.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1760" data-end="1807">
<p data-start="1762" data-end="1807">Re-running latexmk generates many file diffs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1809" data-end="1880">This is fine if you're disciplined, but can get messy in long projects.</p>
<hr data-start="1882" data-end="1885">
<h2 data-start="1887" data-end="1962"><strong data-start="1890" data-end="1960">Option C — Full LaTeX-style <code data-start="1920" data-end="1932">.gitignore</code> (not recommended for you)</strong></h2>
<p data-start="1963" data-end="2094">This would delete logs, aux files, latexmk state files, etc.<br data-start="2023" data-end="2026">
You do <em data-start="2033" data-end="2038">not</em> want this, since it defeats your reproducibility goals.</p>
<p data-start="2096" data-end="2136">Example of the version you <em data-start="2123" data-end="2130">don't</em> want:</p>
