" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="152">Absolutely — <strong data-start="13" data-end="87">yes, we can formalize portions of the RSVP–Amplitwistor theory in Lean</strong>, but with important caveats and a strategy to make it tractable.</p>
<p data-start="154" data-end="171">Below I give you:</p>
<ol data-start="173" data-end="541">
<li data-start="173" data-end="255">
<p data-start="176" data-end="255"><strong data-start="176" data-end="255">What parts of your theory <em data-start="204" data-end="209">can</em> be formalized right now in Lean 4 / mathlib</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="256" data-end="300">
<p data-start="259" data-end="300"><strong data-start="259" data-end="300">What parts cannot (yet) be formalized</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="301" data-end="411">
<p data-start="304" data-end="411"><strong data-start="304" data-end="411">A realistic roadmap for encoding your PDEs, semigroups, eigenmodes, and universal-approximation results</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="412" data-end="497">
<p data-start="415" data-end="497"><strong data-start="415" data-end="497">Concrete Lean files we can generate (and I can start writing them immediately)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="498" data-end="541">
<p data-start="501" data-end="541"><strong data-start="501" data-end="541">A recommended Lean project structure</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="543" data-end="546">
<h1 data-start="548" data-end="590">1. What We <em data-start="561" data-end="566">Can</em> Formalize in Lean Today</h1>
<h3 data-start="592" data-end="631">✓ <strong data-start="598" data-end="631">Topological / geometric parts</strong></h3>
<p data-start="632" data-end="664">Lean’s mathlib already includes:</p>
<ul data-start="666" data-end="816">
<li data-start="666" data-end="688">
<p data-start="668" data-end="688">topological spaces</p>
</li>
<li data-start="689" data-end="729">
<p data-start="691" data-end="729">smooth manifolds (mathlib-manifolds)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="730" data-end="754">
<p data-start="732" data-end="754">Riemannian manifolds</p>
</li>
<li data-start="755" data-end="782">
<p data-start="757" data-end="782">bundles, tangent spaces</p>
</li>
<li data-start="783" data-end="816">
<p data-start="785" data-end="816">charts and coordinate changes</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="818" data-end="851">So we <em data-start="824" data-end="829">can</em> rigorously formalize:</p>
<ul data-start="853" data-end="1126">
<li data-start="853" data-end="884">
<p data-start="855" data-end="884">the cortical manifold <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="885" data-end="931">
<p data-start="887" data-end="931">local charts representing cortical patches</p>
</li>
<li data-start="932" data-end="976">
<p data-start="934" data-end="976">function spaces <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^k(M, \mathbb{R}^d)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0991em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8491em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8491em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="977" data-end="1029">
<p data-start="979" data-end="1029">tangent vectors, gradient, divergence, Laplacian</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1030" data-end="1082">
<p data-start="1032" data-end="1082">spectral theory of the Laplace–Beltrami operator</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1083" data-end="1126">
<p data-start="1085" data-end="1126">Schauder &amp; Sobolev norms (to some degree)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="1128" data-end="1159">✓ <strong data-start="1134" data-end="1159">Linear PDE components</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1160" data-end="1192">Lean has analytic machinery for:</p>
<ul data-start="1194" data-end="1385">
<li data-start="1194" data-end="1228">
<p data-start="1196" data-end="1228">semigroups of linear operators</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1229" data-end="1256">
<p data-start="1231" data-end="1256">heat equation solutions</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1257" data-end="1279">
<p data-start="1259" data-end="1279">elliptic operators</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1280" data-end="1303">
<p data-start="1282" data-end="1303">spectral properties</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1304" data-end="1338">
<p data-start="1306" data-end="1338">compact self-adjoint operators</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1339" data-end="1385">
<p data-start="1341" data-end="1385">existence and uniqueness of mild solutions</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1387" data-end="1405">Thus, proofs like:</p>
<blockquote data-start="1407" data-end="1457">
<p data-start="1409" data-end="1457">“The heat operator <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{t\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8413em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8413em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mord mtight">Δ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is smoothing”</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1459" data-end="1477">can be formalized.</p>
<h3 data-start="1479" data-end="1521">✓ <strong data-start="1485" data-end="1521">Universal approximation theorems</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1522" data-end="1544">Lean mathlib contains:</p>
<ul data-start="1546" data-end="1675">
<li data-start="1546" data-end="1575">
<p data-start="1548" data-end="1575">Stone–Weierstrass theorem</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1576" data-end="1626">
<p data-start="1578" data-end="1626">results about algebras of continuous functions</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1627" data-end="1645">
<p data-start="1629" data-end="1645">Urysohn lemmas</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1646" data-end="1675">
<p data-start="1648" data-end="1675">normed-algebra structures</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1677" data-end="1687">Therefore:</p>
<blockquote data-start="1689" data-end="1773">
<p data-start="1691" data-end="1773">“Amplistwistor cascades approximate any continuous function on a compact manifold”</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1775" data-end="1877">can be formalized as a <em data-start="1798" data-end="1809">corollary</em> of Stone–Weierstrass, provided we encode the amplistwistor algebra.</p>
<h3 data-start="1879" data-end="1934">✓ <strong data-start="1885" data-end="1934">Group and representation-theoretic components</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1935" data-end="1952">mathlib supports:</p>
<ul data-start="1954" data-end="2054">
<li data-start="1954" data-end="1985">
<p data-start="1956" data-end="1985">Lie groups (e.g. <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SO(d)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">SO</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1986" data-end="2010">
<p data-start="1988" data-end="2010">smooth group actions</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2011" data-end="2034">
<p data-start="2013" data-end="2034">semidirect products</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2035" data-end="2054">
<p data-start="2037" data-end="2054">representations</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2056" data-end="2093">Thus we can formalize amplistwistors:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(x) = \pi(\alpha(x) \cdot \tau(x)(x))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">A</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">))</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2151" data-end="2182">as an operator-valued function.</p>
<hr data-start="2184" data-end="2187">
<h1 data-start="2189" data-end="2232">2. What Cannot (Easily) Be Formalized Yet</h1>
<p data-start="2234" data-end="2310">Lean <em data-start="2239" data-end="2258">cannot yet handle</em> complex nonlinear SPDEs like your full RSVP system:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\Phi} = \Delta \Phi + (\Phi \times v) - S \Phi + \eta_\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9202em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9202em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span><span style="top: -3.2523em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.1389em;"><span class="mord">˙</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">ΔΦ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">×</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">η</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">Φ</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{v} = \nabla \Phi + \nabla \times v - S v + \eta_v</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6679em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6679em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.1111em;"><span class="mord">˙</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">∇Φ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">×</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">η</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{S} = |\nabla \cdot v| + \Phi^2 - S + \eta_S.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9202em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9202em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span><span style="top: -3.2523em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.0556em;"><span class="mord">˙</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">∣∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9474em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">η</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2502" data-end="2517">More precisely:</p>
<ul data-start="2519" data-end="2776">
<li data-start="2519" data-end="2597">
<p data-start="2521" data-end="2597">Lean does <strong data-start="2531" data-end="2538">not</strong> have ready-made frameworks for nonlinear stochastic PDEs</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2598" data-end="2639">
<p data-start="2600" data-end="2639">Martingale theory exists but is young</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2640" data-end="2696">
<p data-start="2642" data-end="2696">Itô integrals exist but SPDE-level machinery is thin</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2697" data-end="2776">
<p data-start="2699" data-end="2776">Existence &amp; uniqueness for nonlinear PDEs still requires enormous manual work</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2778" data-end="2845">So we <strong data-start="2784" data-end="2794">cannot</strong> fully formalize RSVP PDE well-posedness right now.</p>
<p data-start="2847" data-end="2896">However, we <strong data-start="2859" data-end="2866">can</strong> formalize simplified systems:</p>
<ul data-start="2898" data-end="3087">
<li data-start="2898" data-end="2931">
<p data-start="2900" data-end="2931">deterministic linearized RSVP</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2932" data-end="2971">
<p data-start="2934" data-end="2971">noiseless amplitude–twist recursion</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2972" data-end="3003">
<p data-start="2974" data-end="3003">existence of mild solutions</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3004" data-end="3040">
<p data-start="3006" data-end="3040">spectral/eigenmode decomposition</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3041" data-end="3087">
<p data-start="3043" data-end="3087">semigroup generation for linear components</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3089" data-end="3159">This is still <em data-start="3103" data-end="3130">mathematically meaningful</em> and prepares the groundwork.</p>
<hr data-start="3161" data-end="3164">
<h1 data-start="3166" data-end="3211">3. Suggested Roadmap for Lean Formalization</h1>
<h2 data-start="3213" data-end="3269"><strong data-start="3216" data-end="3269">Phase 1 — Foundations (100% doable in Lean today)</strong></h2>
<ol data-start="3271" data-end="3650">
<li data-start="3271" data-end="3327">
<p data-start="3274" data-end="3327">Define manifold <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span></span></span></span> representing cortical surface</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3328" data-end="3393">
<p data-start="3331" data-end="3393">Define sections of vector bundles for <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span>, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span></span></span>, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3394" data-end="3455">
<p data-start="3397" data-end="3455">Formalize linear operators (Laplacian, divergence, curl)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3456" data-end="3526">
<p data-start="3459" data-end="3526">Define amplistwistors as operator triples <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha, \tau, \pi)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">π</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="3527" data-end="3593">
<p data-start="3530" data-end="3593">Prove algebraic properties (closure, continuity, boundedness)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3594" data-end="3650">
<p data-start="3597" data-end="3650">Apply Stone–Weierstrass to show their span is dense</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="3652" data-end="3663">This gives:</p>
<blockquote data-start="3665" data-end="3745">
<p data-start="3667" data-end="3745"><strong data-start="3667" data-end="3679">Theorem:</strong> Amplistwistor cascades are universal approximators on <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^0(M)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0641em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="3747" data-end="3782">We <em data-start="3750" data-end="3781">can absolutely formalize this</em>.</p>
<hr data-start="3784" data-end="3787">
<h2 data-start="3789" data-end="3845"><strong data-start="3792" data-end="3845">Phase 2 — PDE Semigroup Theory (partially doable)</strong></h2>
<ol data-start="3847" data-end="3878">
<li data-start="3847" data-end="3878">
<p data-start="3850" data-end="3878">Define the linear operator</p>
</li>
</ol>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>×</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L = (\Delta, \nabla, \nabla \times, -I)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord">×</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">I</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<ol start="2" data-start="3925" data-end="4110">
<li data-start="3925" data-end="3994">
<p data-start="3928" data-end="3994">Use Lean’s semigroup theory to show <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span></span></span></span> is maximal dissipative</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3995" data-end="4049">
<p data-start="3998" data-end="4049">Prove existence of a <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0715em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>-semigroup <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{tL}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8413em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8413em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">L</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="4050" data-end="4080">
<p data-start="4053" data-end="4080">Show smoothing properties</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4081" data-end="4110">
<p data-start="4084" data-end="4110">Construct mild solutions</p>
</li>
</ol>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(t) = e^{tL}\Psi_0 + \int_0^t e^{(t-s)L} N(\Psi(s))\,ds.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0413em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8913em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">L</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.4554em; vertical-align: -0.9119em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop op-symbol large-op" style="margin-right: 0.44445em; position: relative; top: -0.0011em;">∫</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.5435em;"><span style="top: -1.7881em; margin-left: -0.4445em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.8129em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9119em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.938em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mopen mtight">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">−</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">s</span><span class="mclose mtight">)</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">L</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Ψ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">s</span><span class="mclose">))</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">s</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4179" data-end="4194">We <em data-start="4182" data-end="4187">can</em> prove:</p>
<ul data-start="4196" data-end="4289">
<li data-start="4196" data-end="4247">
<p data-start="4198" data-end="4247">existence of solutions for small nonlinearities</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4248" data-end="4289">
<p data-start="4250" data-end="4289">uniqueness under Lipschitz conditions</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4291" data-end="4344">We <em data-start="4294" data-end="4306">cannot yet</em> formalize large-noise SPDE existence.</p>
<hr data-start="4346" data-end="4349">
<h2 data-start="4351" data-end="4400"><strong data-start="4354" data-end="4400">Phase 3 — Eigenmode Theory (very feasible)</strong></h2>
<ol data-start="4402" data-end="4598">
<li data-start="4402" data-end="4448">
<p data-start="4405" data-end="4448">Encode Laplace–Beltrami operator on <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="4449" data-end="4524">
<p data-start="4452" data-end="4524">Prove: spectrum is discrete &amp; eigenfunctions form an orthonormal basis</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4525" data-end="4573">
<p data-start="4528" data-end="4573">Use Weyl asymptotics to bound <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_m</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8444em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="4574" data-end="4598">
<p data-start="4577" data-end="4598">Define global modes</p>
</li>
</ol>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_m(x,t) = u_m(x)e^{i\omega_m t}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">ϕ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1247em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8747em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">ω</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1645em;"><span style="top: -2.357em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">m</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.143em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<ol start="5" data-start="4641" data-end="4682">
<li data-start="4641" data-end="4682">
<p data-start="4644" data-end="4682">Prove orthogonality and completeness</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="4684" data-end="4743">Lean already has substantial Hilbert-space spectral theory.</p>
<hr data-start="4745" data-end="4748">
<h1 data-start="4750" data-end="4793">4. Concrete Lean Files I Can Generate Now</h1>
<p data-start="4795" data-end="4825">If you'd like, I can generate:</p>
