ax-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="29b1b228-2028-4fee-9c23-f03515b8d237" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-1-thinking"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="127">Let’s make the amplitwistor algebra less ghostly and more like a real object you could actually push through Stone–Weierstrass.</p>
<p data-start="129" data-end="157">I will do this in two steps:</p>
<ol data-start="159" data-end="521">
<li data-start="159" data-end="303">
<p data-start="162" data-end="303">Refine <code data-start="169" data-end="197">Amplistwistor/Algebra.lean</code> so there is a concrete algebra in <code data-start="232" data-end="241">C(M, ℝ)</code> built from amplitwistor actions and coordinate functionals.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="304" data-end="521">
<p data-start="307" data-end="521">Update <code data-start="314" data-end="350">Amplistwistor/UniversalApprox.lean</code> to state a realistic universal approximation theorem in terms of that algebra, with proper hypotheses for Stone–Weierstrass (still leaving <code data-start="490" data-end="497">sorry</code> for the heavy lifting).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="523" data-end="609">I will assume the previous <code data-start="550" data-end="577">Amplistwistor.Definitions</code> file is present as we wrote it.</p>
<hr data-start="611" data-end="614">
<p data-start="616" data-end="826">Here is an improved <code data-start="636" data-end="664">Amplistwistor/Algebra.lean</code>. This version constructs a set of basic real-valued functions from amplitwistor-transformed fields and then takes the algebraic closure via <code data-start="805" data-end="825">Subalgebra.closure</code>.</p>
