ken-text-primary h-3 w-3 rounded-full"></div></div><div class="relative my-1 min-h-6"><div class="origin-top-start relative flex flex-col gap-2 overflow-x-clip" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><div class="relative w-full text-start"><div class="flex w-full flex-row items-start justify-between gap-4 text-start"><button class="flex min-w-0 shrink-1 items-center gap-0.5"><span class="font-medium w-full"><span class="flex items-center gap-1 truncate text-start align-middle text-token-text-secondary hover:text-token-text-primary dark:hover:text-token-text-primary dark:text-[var(--interactive-label-tertiary-default)]" style="opacity: 1;"><div class="truncate">Thought for 52s</div></span></span></button></div></div><div class="max-w-[calc(0.8*var(--thread-content-max-width,40rem))]"></div></div></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="d5722622-5292-4c9e-b73d-19aed9267a99" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-1-thinking"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="160">Nice, this is a good direction: a higher-dimensional finite example that actually uses a vector-valued field space, but is still tame enough to fully formalize.</p>
<p data-start="162" data-end="241">Below is a complete Lean module <code data-start="194" data-end="235">Amplistwistor/Example_FiniteVector.lean</code> that:</p>
<ul data-start="243" data-end="891">
<li data-start="243" data-end="321">
<p data-start="245" data-end="321">takes the base space <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M = \mathrm{Fin}\,n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Fin</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span> (finite, compact, Hausdorff),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="322" data-end="398">
<p data-start="324" data-end="398">uses a vector-valued field space <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi>d</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F = \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to \mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Fin</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6889em;"></span><span class="mord mathbb">R</span></span></span></span>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="399" data-end="443">
<p data-start="401" data-end="443">defines coordinate functionals on <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span></span></span></span>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="444" data-end="538">
<p data-start="446" data-end="538">defines a family of base fields that populate individual coordinates at individual points,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="539" data-end="612">
<p data-start="541" data-end="612">builds the amplitwistor-generated subalgebra in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(M, \mathbb{R})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="613" data-end="704">
<p data-start="615" data-end="704">proves that this algebra contains all point-indicator functions and thus all constants,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="705" data-end="735">
<p data-start="707" data-end="735">shows it separates points,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="736" data-end="891">
<p data-start="738" data-end="891">and finally proves that the amplitwistor algebra is the entire <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(M, \mathbb{R})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> (exact universal approximation in this finite vector-valued setting).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="893" data-end="914">You can drop this as:</p>
<p data-start="916" data-end="957"><code data-start="916" data-end="957">Amplistwistor/Example_FiniteVector.lean</code></p>
