<p data-start="1509" data-end="1534"><code data-start="1509" data-end="1529">Continuous.map_add</code> etc.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1536" data-end="1539">
<h1 data-start="1541" data-end="1606">✔ <strong data-start="1545" data-end="1606">B. Graph / Cortical-Surface Discretized Version (in Lean)</strong></h1>
<p data-start="1608" data-end="1650">After the manifold case, I will construct:</p>
<h3 data-start="1652" data-end="1666">1. A file:</h3>
<ul data-start="1667" data-end="1695">
<li data-start="1667" data-end="1695">
<p data-start="1669" data-end="1695"><code data-start="1669" data-end="1695">Amplistwistor/Graph.lean</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1697" data-end="1739">This will interpret the cortical sheet as:</p>
<ul data-start="1741" data-end="1845">
<li data-start="1741" data-end="1771">
<p data-start="1743" data-end="1771">a weighted undirected graph,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1772" data-end="1801">
<p data-start="1774" data-end="1801">or a 2D simplicial complex,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1802" data-end="1845">
<p data-start="1804" data-end="1845">or a mesh derived from neuroimaging data.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="1847" data-end="1861">2. Define:</h3>
<ul data-start="1862" data-end="2055">
<li data-start="1862" data-end="1880">
<p data-start="1864" data-end="1880">graph Laplacian,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1881" data-end="1912">
<p data-start="1883" data-end="1912">eigenvectors as basis fields,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1913" data-end="1972">
<p data-start="1915" data-end="1972">amplitwistor actions on node fields (finite dimensional),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1973" data-end="2004">
<p data-start="1975" data-end="2004">local functional evaluations,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2005" data-end="2055">
<p data-start="2007" data-end="2055">recursive cascades analogous to message passing.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="2057" data-end="2070">3. Prove:</h3>
<ul data-start="2071" data-end="2262">
<li data-start="2071" data-end="2262">
<p data-start="2073" data-end="2262">The amplitwistor algebra spans the full function space <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^N</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8413em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8413em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br data-start="2146" data-end="2149">
(where N is number of nodes),<br data-start="2180" data-end="2183">
essentially generalizing the finite-vector proof you and I already finalized.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="2264" data-end="2290">4. Additional results:</h3>
<ul data-start="2291" data-end="2480">
<li data-start="2291" data-end="2370">
<p data-start="2293" data-end="2370">A spectral graph version of Stone–Weierstrass (equating density to full span)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2371" data-end="2409">
<p data-start="2373" data-end="2409">Projection operators onto eigenmodes</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2410" data-end="2480">
<p data-start="2412" data-end="2480">Universal approximation in the space of signals on the cortical mesh</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2482" data-end="2485">
<h1 data-start="2487" data-end="2542">✔ <strong data-start="2491" data-end="2542">Before proceeding, I need to confirm one choice</strong></h1>
