v class="relative my-1 min-h-6"><div class="origin-top-start relative flex flex-col gap-2 overflow-x-clip" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><div class="relative w-full text-start"><div class="flex w-full flex-row items-start justify-between gap-4 text-start"><button class="flex min-w-0 shrink-1 items-center gap-0.5"><span class="font-medium w-full"><span class="flex items-center gap-1 truncate text-start align-middle text-token-text-secondary hover:text-token-text-primary dark:hover:text-token-text-primary dark:text-[var(--interactive-label-tertiary-default)]" style="opacity: 1;"><div class="truncate">Thought for 34s</div></span></span></button></div></div><div class="max-w-[calc(0.8*var(--thread-content-max-width,40rem))]"></div></div></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="5062c1d4-9e01-473f-8df2-932e0ae69880" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-1-thinking"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="93">Great, let’s build a <strong data-start="21" data-end="56">concrete instantiation skeleton</strong> that mirrors your FOL axioms but is:</p>
<ul data-start="95" data-end="199">
<li data-start="95" data-end="115">
<p data-start="97" data-end="115"><strong data-start="97" data-end="115">self-contained</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="116" data-end="144">
<p data-start="118" data-end="144"><strong data-start="118" data-end="144">beginner-friendly Lean</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="145" data-end="199">
<p data-start="147" data-end="199">and easy to later refit with real amplitwistor math.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="201" data-end="213">The idea is:</p>
<ol data-start="215" data-end="731">
<li data-start="215" data-end="356">
<p data-start="218" data-end="356">Define a <code data-start="227" data-end="234">Model</code> structure that <em data-start="250" data-end="263">packages up</em> all the ingredients from the FOL theory (types, functions, predicates, axioms) in one place.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="357" data-end="612">
<p data-start="360" data-end="399">Give a <strong data-start="367" data-end="392">toy concrete instance</strong> where:</p>
<ul data-start="403" data-end="612">
<li data-start="403" data-end="440">
<p data-start="405" data-end="440">columns are a finite set (<code data-start="431" data-end="438">Fin n</code>),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="444" data-end="491">
<p data-start="446" data-end="491">fields are finite real vectors (<code data-start="478" data-end="489">Fin d → ℝ</code>),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="495" data-end="548">
<p data-start="497" data-end="548">transformations are just functions <code data-start="532" data-end="547">Field → Field</code>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="552" data-end="612">
<p data-start="554" data-end="612">and all axioms are satisfied in a trivial but correct way.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="613" data-end="731">
<p data-start="616" data-end="731">Later, you can replace the toy proofs with real ones (Lipschitz, locality, etc.) using your amplitwistor machinery.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="733" data-end="759">Save this as, for example:</p>
<p data-start="761" data-end="795"><code data-start="761" data-end="795">Amplistwistor/ConcreteModel.lean</code></p>
