<h1 data-start="636" data-end="714"><strong data-start="638" data-end="714">Discretized Dynamics and Numerical Realizations of Amplitwistor Cascades</strong></h1>
<p data-start="716" data-end="802">\section{Discrete Field Evolution and Numerical Realizations of Amplitwistor Cascades}</p>
<p data-start="804" data-end="1652">Although the RSVP framework is formulated in the language of smooth manifolds, tensor fields, and coupled partial differential equations, any operational semantics intended for computation---whether in Lean, in SpherePop, or in numerical experimentation---must eventually admit a discrete representation. The passage from continuous fields to finite grids is not merely a matter of engineering convenience; rather, it provides an alternative viewpoint on the same dynamics, revealing their underlying modularity, stability properties, and compatibility with operadic composition. This section provides a mathematical justification for the discrete structures introduced in the Lean implementation, showing how Gaussian kernels, explicit Euler stepping, and local stencil operators arise naturally from the principles governing RSVP field evolution.</p>
<p data-start="1654" data-end="1707">\subsection{Finite Grid Approximation of RSVP Fields}</p>
