37 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre!"><span><span>\section{Introduction}

Cortical computation exhibits a striking combination </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">of</span></span><span> discrete event-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">like</span></span><span> structure </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> continuous field-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">like</span></span><span> propagation. </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">Local</span></span><span> perturbations such </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">as</span></span><span> synaptic activations initiate cascades </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">of</span></span><span> activity that diffuse, resonate, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> contribute </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">large</span></span><span>-scale coherent patterns across the cortex. Empirical studies across electrophysiology, ECoG, MEG, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> ultrafast fMRI have repeatedly demonstrated that cortical dynamics possess </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">both</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">local</span></span><span> nonlinear sensitivity </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">global</span></span><span> mode-structured organization \citep{Breakspear2017, Cabral2023, Roberts2019}.

This paper advances a unified framework </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> which amplitwistor cascades</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">---structured nonlinear transformations applied at discrete events---serve as generators of cortical activity, while continuous dynamics are governed by semigroup evolution induced by diffusion-like RSVP field operators. These components are integrated operadically, yielding a hierarchical and compositional model capable of capturing both local and global neural dynamics.</span></span><span>
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
