37 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre!"><span><span>\section{Background </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> Cortical Dynamics </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> Neuroscience}

A substantial body </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">of</span></span><span> empirical evidence supports the interpretation </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">of</span></span><span> cortical activity </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">as</span></span><span> a combination </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">of</span></span><span> traveling waves, resonant eigenmodes, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> hierarchical temporal integration \citep{Singer1999, Honey2010, Cabral2023}. Functional connectivity studies reveal that long-range coordination can often be expressed through the eigenmodes </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">of</span></span><span> the structural connectome, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">while</span></span><span> high-resolution imaging captures spatially coherent activation patterns consistent </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">with</span></span><span> diffusive </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">or</span></span><span> wave-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">like</span></span><span> propagation.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">In</span></span><span> parallel, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">language</span></span><span> processing </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> other high-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">level</span></span><span> cognitive </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">functions</span></span><span> exhibit characteristic temporal hierarchies, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">with</span></span><span> deeper cortical regions integrating information </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">over</span></span><span> longer timescales \citep{Goldstein2025}. These findings motivate a mathematical framework that accounts simultaneously </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">local</span></span><span> nonlinear interactions, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">global</span></span><span> modal structure, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">recursive</span></span><span> temporal evolution.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
