The TARTAN mechanism introduces </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">recursive</span></span><span> structure </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">into</span></span><span> RSVP field evolution </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">by</span></span><span> subdividing trajectories </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">into</span></span><span> tiled regions equipped </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">with</span></span><span> annotated noise </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> boundary-aware smoothing rules. This recursion enables hierarchical refinement </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">of</span></span><span> field configurations </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> models the multiscale evolution </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">of</span></span><span> neural representations. </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">In</span></span><span> combination </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">with</span></span><span> amplitwistor cascades, TARTAN provides a means </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> composing structured perturbations </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> ways that reflect </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">both</span></span><span> temporal recursion </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> spatial locality.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
