Amplistwistors generalize Needham</span><span><span class="hljs-symbol">'s</span></span><span> amplitwist interpretation of complex derivatives \citep{Needham1997} to multidimensional cortical fields. Each amplitwistor acts </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">as</span></span><span> a nonlinear operator combining amplitude modulation, rotational transformation, and projection. These operators serve </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">as</span></span><span> the discrete ``primitives'' </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title class_">constructing</span></span><span> cascades of localized perturbations. Their algebraic structure aligns naturally with the operadic semantics of SpherePop processes and provides a powerful tool </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title class_">encoding</span></span><span> nonlinear transformations </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> cortical computation.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
